1
00:00:07,020 --> 00:00:12,620
Listen, practice, speak. Practice makes you perfect.

2
00:00:12,620 --> 00:00:18,150
Hello, and welcome back to the Business English podcast.

3
00:00:18,150 --> 00:00:21,050
Hi, everyone, and thank you for joining us today.

4
00:00:21,050 --> 00:00:27,250
We're really excited because today's episode is going to be incredibly practical, detailed,

5
00:00:27,250 --> 00:00:29,850
and full of real-life examples.

6
00:00:29,850 --> 00:00:32,050
Absolutely. I'm Leo.

7
00:00:32,050 --> 00:00:37,250
And I'm Tina. And as always, we're here to help you speak English more naturally,

8
00:00:37,250 --> 00:00:42,050
more confidently, and more effectively in real life situations.

9
00:00:42,050 --> 00:00:47,050
Today's topic is something many people experience at least once in their life.

10
00:00:47,050 --> 00:00:48,950
Sometimes, many times.

11
00:00:48,950 --> 00:00:54,350
We're talking about changing your job and how to talk about it in business English.

12
00:00:54,350 --> 00:00:57,850
Yes, and this is not just about vocabulary.

13
00:00:57,850 --> 00:01:00,150
It's about real conversations.

14
00:01:00,150 --> 00:01:03,450
What you say to your friends, your boss, your colleagues,

15
00:01:03,450 --> 00:01:07,050
and even yourself when you're thinking about making a change.

16
00:01:07,050 --> 00:01:14,850
Exactly. Changing your job is a big decision. It can be exciting, stressful, confusing, and

17
00:01:14,850 --> 00:01:17,330
sometimes even emotional.

18
00:01:17,330 --> 00:01:22,690
And if you want to talk about all of that in English, you need the right words, phrases,

19
00:01:22,690 --> 00:01:24,130
and confidence.

20
00:01:24,130 --> 00:01:29,770
So today, we're going to walk you through a full journey from feeling unhappy in your

21
00:01:29,770 --> 00:01:35,290
current job to searching for a new one, going through interviews, resigning, and

22
00:01:35,290 --> 00:01:41,370
starting fresh. And we'll include practical examples, natural conversations, and

23
00:01:41,370 --> 00:01:46,370
even some mistakes people make so you can avoid them. Sounds like a full

24
00:01:46,370 --> 00:01:52,330
experience. It really is. So grab your coffee, relax, and let's get started.

25
00:01:52,330 --> 00:01:56,970
Tina, let me ask you something. Have you ever seriously thought about

26
00:01:56,970 --> 00:02:03,970
Oh yes, many times. I think it's very normal. At some point, you start asking yourself questions like,

27
00:02:03,970 --> 00:02:07,970
Am I happy here? Or is this what I want long term?

28
00:02:07,970 --> 00:02:13,970
That's true. I remember a time when I woke up on a Monday morning and just thought,

29
00:02:13,970 --> 00:02:15,970
I don't want to do this anymore.

30
00:02:15,970 --> 00:02:21,970
That feeling is very common. And in English, you can express it in many ways.

31
00:02:21,970 --> 00:02:27,530
For example, I feel stuck, or I'm not satisfied with my current role.

32
00:02:27,530 --> 00:02:31,750
I like that phrase, I'm not satisfied with my current role.

33
00:02:31,750 --> 00:02:33,250
It sounds professional.

34
00:02:33,250 --> 00:02:39,570
Yes, it's much better than saying I hate my job, especially in professional conversations.

35
00:02:39,570 --> 00:02:44,370
So let's imagine someone is starting to think about changing jobs.

36
00:02:44,370 --> 00:02:46,650
What's the first thing they might say?

37
00:02:46,650 --> 00:02:50,930
They might say, I've been thinking about changing jobs lately.

38
00:02:50,930 --> 00:02:54,010
Or, I'm considering a career change.

39
00:02:54,010 --> 00:02:57,090
Yes, that's another great phrase.

40
00:02:57,090 --> 00:02:59,450
Considering sounds thoughtful and careful.

41
00:02:59,450 --> 00:03:01,090
And what about reasons?

42
00:03:01,090 --> 00:03:04,370
Why do people usually want to change jobs?

43
00:03:04,370 --> 00:03:05,890
There are many reasons.

44
00:03:05,890 --> 00:03:09,570
For example, I want better work-life balance.

45
00:03:09,570 --> 00:03:11,210
That's a big one.

46
00:03:11,210 --> 00:03:12,210
Very big.

47
00:03:12,210 --> 00:03:14,730
Or, I'm looking for new challenges.

48
00:03:14,730 --> 00:03:17,570
I hear that phrase a lot in interviews.

49
00:03:17,570 --> 00:03:24,130
Yes. It's very common and very safe. Another one is, there's no room for growth.

50
00:03:24,130 --> 00:03:27,490
That one is powerful. It shows ambition.

51
00:03:27,490 --> 00:03:32,690
Exactly. It means you want to develop your skills and move forward in your career.

52
00:03:32,690 --> 00:03:36,850
Let me try an example. I've learned a lot in my current job,

53
00:03:36,850 --> 00:03:39,650
but I feel there's no room for growth.

54
00:03:39,650 --> 00:03:42,610
Perfect. That sounds natural and professional.

55
00:03:42,610 --> 00:03:46,130
What about salary? Can people say that directly?

56
00:03:46,130 --> 00:03:49,010
Yes, but carefully. You can say,

57
00:03:49,010 --> 00:03:52,210
I'm looking for a better compensation package.

58
00:03:52,210 --> 00:03:56,130
That sounds much more professional than I want more money.

59
00:03:56,130 --> 00:03:58,370
Exactly. You can also say,

60
00:03:58,370 --> 00:04:02,850
I don't feel that my current salary reflects my responsibilities.

61
00:04:02,850 --> 00:04:05,410
That's a very smart way to say it.

62
00:04:05,410 --> 00:04:08,690
Now let's talk about another important situation.

63
00:04:08,690 --> 00:04:11,570
Talking to a friend about changing jobs.

64
00:04:11,570 --> 00:04:14,210
That's usually more relaxed, right?

65
00:04:14,210 --> 00:04:18,410
Yes. For example, I'm thinking about quitting my job.

66
00:04:18,410 --> 00:04:20,710
Or I need a change.

67
00:04:20,710 --> 00:04:24,110
Exactly. Or even I'm burned out.

68
00:04:24,110 --> 00:04:25,810
That's a strong one.

69
00:04:25,810 --> 00:04:32,110
Yes. Burned out means you're very tired mentally and emotionally because of work.

70
00:04:32,110 --> 00:04:34,110
I remember saying that once.

71
00:04:34,110 --> 00:04:38,310
I said, I feel completely burned out. I need a break.

72
00:04:38,310 --> 00:04:41,110
That's very real and very honest.

73
00:04:41,110 --> 00:04:46,150
So, after someone decides they want to change jobs, what's next?

74
00:04:46,150 --> 00:04:47,950
The job search begins.

75
00:04:47,950 --> 00:04:50,990
Ah yes, the famous job hunt.

76
00:04:50,990 --> 00:04:52,190
Exactly.

77
00:04:52,190 --> 00:04:55,190
You can say, I've started job hunting.

78
00:04:55,190 --> 00:04:59,110
Or I'm actively looking for new opportunities.

79
00:04:59,110 --> 00:05:02,630
That's a great phrase, especially for professional settings.

80
00:05:02,630 --> 00:05:05,710
So what do people do during a job search?

81
00:05:05,710 --> 00:05:07,990
First, they update their resume.

82
00:05:07,990 --> 00:05:08,990
Right.

83
00:05:08,990 --> 00:05:16,270
to update my resume. And also I'm working on my cover letter. Let's give a practical example.

84
00:05:16,270 --> 00:05:24,030
Imagine I say I updated my resume yesterday and applied for three jobs. Perfect. Very clear and

85
00:05:24,030 --> 00:05:31,550
natural. What about LinkedIn? Yes. People often say I updated my LinkedIn profile or

86
00:05:31,550 --> 00:05:37,150
I'm networking on LinkedIn. Networking is very important. Absolutely.

87
00:05:37,150 --> 00:05:40,510
You can say, I reached out to a few contacts.

88
00:05:40,510 --> 00:05:42,350
That's a great phrase.

89
00:05:42,350 --> 00:05:45,390
Now let's talk about applying for jobs.

90
00:05:45,390 --> 00:05:46,190
Okay.

91
00:05:46,190 --> 00:05:50,510
You can say, I applied for a position at a marketing company.

92
00:05:50,510 --> 00:05:54,110
Or, I submitted my application online.

93
00:05:54,110 --> 00:05:56,990
Yes, and then comes the waiting.

94
00:05:56,990 --> 00:05:58,430
The hardest part.

95
00:05:58,430 --> 00:06:01,470
You can say, I'm waiting to hear back.

96
00:06:01,470 --> 00:06:04,030
Or, I haven't heard back yet.

97
00:06:04,030 --> 00:06:06,670
Exactly. Very common phrases.

98
00:06:06,670 --> 00:06:09,070
Now let's move to interviews.

99
00:06:09,070 --> 00:06:12,430
Yes, the exciting and stressful part.

100
00:06:12,430 --> 00:06:15,230
What do people say before an interview?

101
00:06:15,230 --> 00:06:19,630
I have an interview tomorrow, or I'm preparing for an interview.

102
00:06:19,630 --> 00:06:21,550
And during preparation?

103
00:06:21,550 --> 00:06:23,550
I'm practicing my answers.

104
00:06:23,550 --> 00:06:25,710
Let's simulate a situation.

105
00:06:25,710 --> 00:06:30,190
I say, I have an interview next week and I'm really nervous.

106
00:06:30,190 --> 00:06:32,830
And I might respond, that's normal.

107
00:06:32,830 --> 00:06:35,310
Just be yourself and prepare well.

108
00:06:35,310 --> 00:06:36,430
Good advice.

109
00:06:36,430 --> 00:06:40,750
Now, during the interview, you need to describe your job tasks.

110
00:06:40,750 --> 00:06:42,750
Yes, very important.

111
00:06:42,750 --> 00:06:50,190
For example, in my current role, I manage client accounts, prepare reports, and coordinate with the sales team.

112
00:06:50,190 --> 00:06:51,950
That's a great sentence.

113
00:06:51,950 --> 00:06:54,670
It clearly explains your responsibilities.

114
00:06:54,670 --> 00:06:55,950
Let me try.

115
00:06:55,950 --> 00:07:02,030
I handle customer inquiries, solve problems, and ensure customer satisfaction.

116
00:07:02,030 --> 00:07:04,190
Excellent. Very professional.

117
00:07:04,190 --> 00:07:08,190
What if someone asks, why are you leaving your current job?

118
00:07:08,190 --> 00:07:11,310
You can say, I'm looking for new challenges.

119
00:07:11,310 --> 00:07:14,190
Or, I want to grow professionally.

120
00:07:14,190 --> 00:07:16,910
Yes, avoid negative language.

121
00:07:16,910 --> 00:07:20,190
So don't say, my boss is terrible.

122
00:07:20,190 --> 00:07:21,710
Definitely not.

123
00:07:21,710 --> 00:07:24,350
After the interview, what do people say?

124
00:07:24,350 --> 00:07:25,630
I think it went well.

125
00:07:25,630 --> 00:07:28,590
Or, it was challenging but interesting.

126
00:07:28,590 --> 00:07:29,630
And then?

127
00:07:29,630 --> 00:07:31,070
Waiting again.

128
00:07:31,070 --> 00:07:32,670
Always waiting.

129
00:07:32,670 --> 00:07:34,830
Then comes the job offer.

130
00:07:34,830 --> 00:07:36,150
The best part.

131
00:07:36,150 --> 00:07:39,550
You might hear, we'd like to offer you the position.

132
00:07:39,550 --> 00:07:42,870
And you respond, thank you, I'm very interested.

133
00:07:42,870 --> 00:07:45,190
Then you discuss details.

134
00:07:45,190 --> 00:07:48,350
Like salary, benefits and working hours.

135
00:07:48,350 --> 00:07:52,230
Yes, you can say, I'd like to discuss the salary.

136
00:07:52,230 --> 00:07:55,510
Or is there any flexibility in the offer?

137
00:07:55,510 --> 00:07:57,830
That's a very important phrase.

138
00:07:57,830 --> 00:07:59,630
What about negotiating?

139
00:07:59,630 --> 00:08:02,350
You can say, based on my experience,

140
00:08:02,350 --> 00:08:04,630
I'd like to negotiate the salary.

141
00:08:04,630 --> 00:08:06,310
That sounds confident.

142
00:08:06,310 --> 00:08:08,150
Yes, and professional.

143
00:08:08,150 --> 00:08:11,510
Now comes the difficult part, resigning.

144
00:08:11,510 --> 00:08:13,590
Yes, telling your boss.

145
00:08:13,590 --> 00:08:15,430
What's a good way to start?

146
00:08:15,430 --> 00:08:18,350
I'd like to talk to you about something important.

147
00:08:18,350 --> 00:08:21,270
Then I've decided to move on.

148
00:08:21,270 --> 00:08:23,310
That's a very polite phrase.

149
00:08:23,310 --> 00:08:27,550
Yes, you can also say, I've accepted another position.

150
00:08:27,550 --> 00:08:30,110
And I'd like to give my notice.

151
00:08:30,110 --> 00:08:31,390
Exactly.

152
00:08:31,390 --> 00:08:33,670
What about showing appreciation?

153
00:08:33,670 --> 00:08:35,110
Very important.

154
00:08:35,110 --> 00:08:37,510
Say, thank you for the opportunity.

155
00:08:37,510 --> 00:08:38,990
I've learned a lot here.

156
00:08:38,990 --> 00:08:41,070
That leaves a good impression.

157
00:08:41,070 --> 00:08:43,830
Yes, always leave on good terms.

158
00:08:43,830 --> 00:08:46,270
Then comes the notice period.

159
00:08:46,270 --> 00:08:50,670
Right, you can say, my last day will be two weeks from today.

160
00:08:50,670 --> 00:08:54,190
And during that time, I'll complete my tasks

161
00:08:54,190 --> 00:08:56,070
and help with the transition.

162
00:08:56,070 --> 00:08:57,430
Very professional.

163
00:08:57,430 --> 00:09:00,390
Finally, the new job begins.

164
00:09:00,390 --> 00:09:01,930
the fresh start.

165
00:09:01,930 --> 00:09:03,970
On your first day, you can say,

166
00:09:03,970 --> 00:09:05,050
nice to meet you.

167
00:09:05,050 --> 00:09:06,730
I'm excited to be here.

168
00:09:06,730 --> 00:09:08,850
Or could you show me around?

169
00:09:08,850 --> 00:09:11,670
Yes, and I'm still learning.

170
00:09:11,670 --> 00:09:13,430
That's a great phrase.

171
00:09:13,430 --> 00:09:15,890
After a few days, you might say,

172
00:09:15,890 --> 00:09:18,010
I'm starting to feel more comfortable.

173
00:09:18,010 --> 00:09:20,330
Or I'm getting the hang of it.

174
00:09:20,330 --> 00:09:21,510
Exactly.

175
00:09:21,510 --> 00:09:24,670
Tina, this has been a very complete journey.

176
00:09:24,670 --> 00:09:28,690
Yes, from feeling unhappy to starting a new job.

177
00:09:28,690 --> 00:09:31,770
and we used so many practical phrases.

178
00:09:31,770 --> 00:09:35,690
That's the goal, to make English useful in real life.

179
00:09:35,690 --> 00:09:39,490
Before we finish, let's ask our listeners a question.

180
00:09:39,490 --> 00:09:44,290
Yes, our question of the day, why would you change your job?

181
00:09:44,290 --> 00:09:47,770
You can answer like this, I would change my job

182
00:09:47,770 --> 00:09:50,890
because I want better work-life balance.

183
00:09:50,890 --> 00:09:53,530
Or I want to learn new skills.

184
00:09:53,530 --> 00:09:56,050
Write your answer, practice your English,

185
00:09:56,050 --> 00:09:57,890
and think about your future.

186
00:09:57,890 --> 00:09:58,970
Exactly.

187
00:09:58,970 --> 00:10:01,570
Thank you so much for listening today.

188
00:10:01,570 --> 00:10:03,810
Keep practicing, keep improving,

189
00:10:03,810 --> 00:10:06,450
and don't be afraid to make changes.

190
00:10:06,450 --> 00:10:07,650
See you later, time.

191
00:10:07,650 --> 00:10:08,770
Goodbye, everyone.

192
00:10:08,770 --> 00:10:12,570
Hello, and welcome back to the Business English Podcast.

193
00:10:12,570 --> 00:10:14,570
Hello, everyone, and thank you so much

194
00:10:14,570 --> 00:10:15,770
for joining us today.

195
00:10:15,770 --> 00:10:17,290
Hi, everyone, welcome back.

196
00:10:17,290 --> 00:10:19,410
We're really excited to have you here.

197
00:10:19,410 --> 00:10:20,250
I'm Daniel.

198
00:10:20,250 --> 00:10:21,290
And I'm Sophia.

199
00:10:21,290 --> 00:10:24,210
On this podcast, we help you improve your English

200
00:10:24,210 --> 00:10:27,610
through natural conversations, real life situations,

201
00:10:27,610 --> 00:10:30,350
and practical examples you can actually use

202
00:10:30,350 --> 00:10:32,570
at work and in your daily life.

203
00:10:32,570 --> 00:10:34,770
Exactly, our goal is simple.

204
00:10:34,770 --> 00:10:38,490
To make English feel natural, useful, and easy to apply.

205
00:10:38,490 --> 00:10:42,110
Not complicated, not stressful, just real communication.

206
00:10:42,110 --> 00:10:45,610
Today's topic is something that almost everyone experiences

207
00:10:45,610 --> 00:10:47,350
at some point in their career.

208
00:10:47,350 --> 00:10:50,570
We're talking about talking about changing your job

209
00:10:50,570 --> 00:10:52,050
in business English.

210
00:10:52,050 --> 00:10:54,690
Yes, and this is such an important topic

211
00:10:54,690 --> 00:10:57,330
because changing jobs is not just about finding

212
00:10:57,330 --> 00:11:01,730
new position. It's about expressing your thoughts clearly, explaining your reasons,

213
00:11:01,730 --> 00:11:05,250
communicating professionally, and making confident decisions.

214
00:11:05,250 --> 00:11:11,010
We're going to walk through the entire journey, from thinking about leaving your job, to applying,

215
00:11:11,010 --> 00:11:15,890
to interviews, to negotiating, resigning, and starting a new role.

216
00:11:15,890 --> 00:11:21,330
And everything will be in conversation format, so you can hear exactly how real English sounds

217
00:11:21,330 --> 00:11:26,290
in real situations. All right, let's begin. Daniel, how are you today?

218
00:11:26,290 --> 00:11:31,250
I'm doing well, thanks. Actually, I've been thinking a lot about career growth lately.

219
00:11:31,250 --> 00:11:33,970
That sounds interesting. What made you think about that?

220
00:11:33,970 --> 00:11:39,490
Well, one of my colleagues recently changed jobs, and he shared his entire experience with me,

221
00:11:39,490 --> 00:11:42,690
from feeling stuck to finally finding a better opportunity.

222
00:11:42,690 --> 00:11:47,250
That's a perfect example. I think many people feel that way at some point.

223
00:11:47,250 --> 00:11:50,930
They reach a stage where they start questioning their current job.

224
00:11:50,930 --> 00:11:56,130
Yes, exactly. So let's imagine someone is at that stage. What can they say in English?

225
00:11:56,130 --> 00:11:58,370
A very natural sentence would be,

226
00:11:58,370 --> 00:12:00,930
I've been thinking about changing my job.

227
00:12:00,930 --> 00:12:02,290
That's simple and clear.

228
00:12:02,290 --> 00:12:03,410
Another option is,

229
00:12:03,410 --> 00:12:05,730
I'm considering a career change.

230
00:12:05,730 --> 00:12:08,370
Yes, and if you want to sound more professional,

231
00:12:08,370 --> 00:12:09,330
you can say,

232
00:12:09,330 --> 00:12:11,410
I'm exploring new opportunities.

233
00:12:11,410 --> 00:12:12,770
I really like that phrase.

234
00:12:12,770 --> 00:12:14,930
It sounds positive and forward-looking.

235
00:12:14,930 --> 00:12:16,210
Absolutely.

236
00:12:16,210 --> 00:12:18,370
Now let's talk about reasons.

237
00:12:18,370 --> 00:12:20,770
Why do people want to change their jobs?

238
00:12:20,770 --> 00:12:22,130
There are many reasons.

239
00:12:22,130 --> 00:12:23,730
One of the most common ones is,

240
00:12:23,730 --> 00:12:25,890
I want better work-life balance.

241
00:12:25,890 --> 00:12:30,130
That's a big one. People don't want to feel exhausted all the time.

242
00:12:30,130 --> 00:12:34,130
Right. Another reason could be, I feel like there's no room to grow.

243
00:12:34,130 --> 00:12:38,130
That means there are no opportunities for promotion or development.

244
00:12:38,130 --> 00:12:42,130
Exactly. You might also hear, I'm not challenged anymore.

245
00:12:42,130 --> 00:12:44,210
Or simply, I feel stuck.

246
00:12:44,210 --> 00:12:49,330
That's very natural. For example, I've been in the same role for years and I feel stuck.

247
00:12:49,330 --> 00:12:51,410
What about stronger feelings?

248
00:12:51,410 --> 00:12:53,970
Then you can say, I'm feeling burned out.

249
00:12:53,970 --> 00:12:55,890
That's an important phrase.

250
00:12:55,890 --> 00:13:00,770
It means you're mentally and emotionally exhausted from too much work or stress.

251
00:13:00,770 --> 00:13:01,770
Yes.

252
00:13:01,770 --> 00:13:06,050
For example, I've been working long hours for months and I feel burned out.

253
00:13:06,050 --> 00:13:09,770
Now let's imagine a real conversation between two friends.

254
00:13:09,770 --> 00:13:10,770
Okay.

255
00:13:10,770 --> 00:13:13,250
Hey, I've been thinking about changing my job.

256
00:13:13,250 --> 00:13:14,250
Oh really?

257
00:13:14,250 --> 00:13:15,250
Why?

258
00:13:15,250 --> 00:13:17,450
I just feel like I need a fresh start.

259
00:13:17,450 --> 00:13:18,610
That's a great phrase.

260
00:13:18,610 --> 00:13:19,810
A fresh start.

261
00:13:19,810 --> 00:13:21,850
It sounds hopeful, not negative.

262
00:13:21,850 --> 00:13:22,970
Exactly.

263
00:13:22,970 --> 00:13:26,330
Another good answer is, I want to try something different.

264
00:13:26,330 --> 00:13:28,330
Or I want a job that fits me better.

265
00:13:28,330 --> 00:13:30,170
That's a nice expression.

266
00:13:30,170 --> 00:13:33,550
It means the job matches your personality and goals.

267
00:13:33,550 --> 00:13:37,210
Now let's move to the next step, preparing for the job change.

268
00:13:37,210 --> 00:13:40,570
The first thing most people do is update their resume.

269
00:13:40,570 --> 00:13:44,010
Yes, you can say I need to update my resume.

270
00:13:44,010 --> 00:13:47,010
And also, I should rewrite my cover letter.

271
00:13:47,010 --> 00:13:50,250
Many people forget about the cover letter, but it's very important.

272
00:13:50,250 --> 00:13:51,250
It is.

273
00:13:51,250 --> 00:13:55,330
helps you explain why you want the job and why you're a good fit.

274
00:13:55,330 --> 00:13:56,330
That frees again.

275
00:13:56,330 --> 00:13:57,330
A good fit.

276
00:13:57,330 --> 00:13:58,330
Yes.

277
00:13:58,330 --> 00:14:00,410
Very important in business English.

278
00:14:00,410 --> 00:14:02,610
After that, you start job hunting.

279
00:14:02,610 --> 00:14:05,010
Job hunting means searching for jobs.

280
00:14:05,010 --> 00:14:07,450
You can say, I'm job hunting right now.

281
00:14:07,450 --> 00:14:10,250
Or I'm applying to several positions.

282
00:14:10,250 --> 00:14:13,310
Or I sent out five applications this week.

283
00:14:13,310 --> 00:14:15,170
That sounds very realistic.

284
00:14:15,170 --> 00:14:16,970
Then comes the waiting stage.

285
00:14:16,970 --> 00:14:17,970
Yes.

286
00:14:17,970 --> 00:14:19,070
The difficult part.

287
00:14:19,070 --> 00:14:21,590
You can say, I'm waiting to hear back.

288
00:14:21,590 --> 00:14:23,950
That means you're waiting for a response.

289
00:14:23,950 --> 00:14:25,950
Then finally you get an interview.

290
00:14:25,950 --> 00:14:28,390
You might say, I got an interview.

291
00:14:28,390 --> 00:14:31,330
Or you can say, they invited me for an interview.

292
00:14:31,330 --> 00:14:34,510
Now let's talk about interview conversations.

293
00:14:34,510 --> 00:14:38,150
One of the most common questions is, can you tell me about yourself?

294
00:14:38,150 --> 00:14:43,390
A simple answer could be, I have three years of experience in customer service and I'm

295
00:14:43,390 --> 00:14:46,150
looking for a new opportunity to grow.

296
00:14:46,150 --> 00:14:47,990
That's clear and professional.

297
00:14:47,990 --> 00:14:50,990
Another question is, why do you want to change your job?

298
00:14:50,990 --> 00:14:53,890
You can say, I'm looking for new challenges.

299
00:14:53,890 --> 00:14:57,390
Or you can say, I want to develop my skills further.

300
00:14:57,390 --> 00:15:01,110
Or I'm interested in a role with more responsibility.

301
00:15:01,110 --> 00:15:03,570
Then they might ask, what are your strengths?

302
00:15:03,570 --> 00:15:05,630
You can say, I'm organized.

303
00:15:05,630 --> 00:15:06,950
I'm a quick learner.

304
00:15:06,950 --> 00:15:08,790
I work well under pressure.

305
00:15:08,790 --> 00:15:11,430
I communicate effectively with others.

306
00:15:11,430 --> 00:15:13,390
Now the difficult one.

307
00:15:13,390 --> 00:15:15,190
What are your weaknesses?

308
00:15:15,190 --> 00:15:20,270
You can say sometimes I take on too much work, but I'm learning to manage my time better.

309
00:15:20,270 --> 00:15:22,890
That shows honesty and improvement.

310
00:15:22,890 --> 00:15:24,550
After the interview, what can you say?

311
00:15:24,550 --> 00:15:26,790
I think the interview went well.

312
00:15:26,790 --> 00:15:31,110
Or you can say I was nervous at first, but I felt more confident later.

313
00:15:31,110 --> 00:15:33,970
Or you can say I hope they call me back.

314
00:15:33,970 --> 00:15:35,830
Then comes the offer stage.

315
00:15:35,830 --> 00:15:39,510
The company might say we'd like to offer you the position.

316
00:15:39,510 --> 00:15:42,010
And you reply thank you for the offer.

317
00:15:42,010 --> 00:15:43,870
Then you ask questions.

318
00:15:43,870 --> 00:15:45,150
What is the salary?

319
00:15:45,150 --> 00:15:46,870
benefits are included.

320
00:15:46,870 --> 00:15:49,390
Is there flexibility in working hours?

321
00:15:49,390 --> 00:15:51,950
Now let's talk about negotiation.

322
00:15:51,950 --> 00:15:55,070
You can say, I'd like to discuss the salary.

323
00:15:55,070 --> 00:15:58,550
Or you can say, is there any flexibility in the offer?

324
00:15:58,550 --> 00:16:03,070
Or you can say, I was hoping for a slightly higher salary.

325
00:16:03,070 --> 00:16:04,750
That's polite and professional.

326
00:16:04,750 --> 00:16:08,990
If you need time, you can say, I'd like some time to think about it.

327
00:16:08,990 --> 00:16:12,030
Then you accept, I'm happy to accept the offer.

328
00:16:12,030 --> 00:16:13,030
Or decline.

329
00:16:13,030 --> 00:16:15,610
I've decided to decline the offer.

330
00:16:15,610 --> 00:16:17,330
Now comes resigning.

331
00:16:17,330 --> 00:16:19,390
The difficult conversation.

332
00:16:19,390 --> 00:16:23,550
You can start with, I'd like to talk to you about something important.

333
00:16:23,550 --> 00:16:25,670
Then I've decided to move on.

334
00:16:25,670 --> 00:16:28,190
Or I've accepted another position.

335
00:16:28,190 --> 00:16:30,510
Then I'd like to give my notice.

336
00:16:30,510 --> 00:16:32,110
Usually two weeks.

337
00:16:32,110 --> 00:16:35,430
You can say my last day will be two weeks from today.

338
00:16:35,430 --> 00:16:37,270
It's important to be respectful.

339
00:16:37,270 --> 00:16:39,910
Yes, say thank you for the opportunity.

340
00:16:39,910 --> 00:16:41,430
I've learned a lot here.

341
00:16:41,430 --> 00:16:43,310
I appreciate your support.

342
00:16:43,310 --> 00:16:45,430
Then you start your new job.

343
00:16:45,430 --> 00:16:46,430
First day.

344
00:16:46,430 --> 00:16:48,470
You say, hi, nice to meet you.

345
00:16:48,470 --> 00:16:50,150
I'm excited to be here.

346
00:16:50,150 --> 00:16:51,470
Could you show me around?

347
00:16:51,470 --> 00:16:53,070
I'm still learning.

348
00:16:53,070 --> 00:16:57,310
After a few days, you can say, I'm starting to feel more comfortable.

349
00:16:57,310 --> 00:16:59,610
Or you can say, I'm getting the hang of it.

350
00:16:59,610 --> 00:17:01,230
That means you're improving.

351
00:17:01,230 --> 00:17:02,230
Exactly.

352
00:17:02,230 --> 00:17:04,910
So changing jobs is a full journey.

353
00:17:04,910 --> 00:17:10,410
Yes, from thinking, to applying, to interviewing, to resigning, to starting again.

354
00:17:10,410 --> 00:17:12,990
And the English you need is actually simple.

355
00:17:12,990 --> 00:17:15,490
Short, clear, useful phrases.

356
00:17:15,490 --> 00:17:17,050
So don't be afraid.

357
00:17:17,050 --> 00:17:18,930
Take it step by step.

358
00:17:18,930 --> 00:17:20,210
Practice these phrases.

359
00:17:20,210 --> 00:17:21,970
Keep building your confidence.

360
00:17:21,970 --> 00:17:24,130
Thank you so much for listening today.

361
00:17:24,130 --> 00:17:28,490
We hope this helps you understand how to talk about changing your job in English.

362
00:17:28,490 --> 00:17:29,610
Keep practicing.

363
00:17:29,610 --> 00:17:30,610
Keep learning.

364
00:17:30,610 --> 00:17:32,330
And we'll see you next time.

365
00:17:32,330 --> 00:17:33,330
Goodbye everyone.

366
00:17:33,330 --> 00:17:36,050
Hello and welcome back to Business English.

367
00:17:36,050 --> 00:17:37,050
Hi everyone.

368
00:17:37,050 --> 00:17:39,650
Welcome to today's English Conversation Practice.

369
00:17:39,650 --> 00:17:40,770
I'm Daniel.

370
00:17:40,770 --> 00:17:42,010
And I'm Sophia.

371
00:17:42,010 --> 00:17:45,010
And we're really happy you're here learning with us today.

372
00:17:45,010 --> 00:17:51,850
Our goal is to help you speak English naturally, confidently, and clearly in real workplace situations.

373
00:17:51,850 --> 00:17:55,290
Today's topic is extremely practical and important.

374
00:17:55,290 --> 00:17:59,690
We're going to talk about how to talk about changing your job in business English.

375
00:17:59,690 --> 00:18:04,490
Yes, this is something many people experience at some point in their career.

376
00:18:04,490 --> 00:18:05,970
Maybe you want better pay.

377
00:18:05,970 --> 00:18:10,050
Maybe you want new challenges, or maybe you just want a fresh start.

378
00:18:10,050 --> 00:18:11,130
Exactly.

379
00:18:11,130 --> 00:18:15,930
And talking about changing jobs in English is not just about saying, I quit.

380
00:18:15,930 --> 00:18:21,490
You need to explain your reasons, your plans, your experience, and your goals in a professional

381
00:18:21,490 --> 00:18:22,490
way.

382
00:18:22,490 --> 00:18:23,490
That's right.

383
00:18:23,490 --> 00:18:27,930
So today, we're going to guide you through real conversations, useful phrases, and practical

384
00:18:27,930 --> 00:18:32,570
examples you can use when thinking about leaving your job, applying for new roles,

385
00:18:32,570 --> 00:18:34,890
interviewing, and starting something new.

386
00:18:34,890 --> 00:18:40,010
So if you're ready to upgrade your business English and talk about your career with confidence,

387
00:18:40,010 --> 00:18:41,010
let's get started.

388
00:18:41,010 --> 00:18:42,890
Daniel, how are you today?

389
00:18:42,890 --> 00:18:44,210
I'm doing well, thanks.

390
00:18:44,210 --> 00:18:46,610
A bit reflective today, actually.

391
00:18:46,610 --> 00:18:47,610
Reflective?

392
00:18:47,610 --> 00:18:48,610
That sounds interesting.

393
00:18:48,610 --> 00:18:49,610
Why is that?

394
00:18:49,610 --> 00:18:54,010
Well, I was thinking about my career path and how many times I considered changing

395
00:18:54,010 --> 00:18:55,010
jobs.

396
00:18:55,010 --> 00:18:57,370
Oh, that's a great connection to today's topic.

397
00:18:57,370 --> 00:19:00,330
I think almost everyone has felt that at some point.

398
00:19:00,330 --> 00:19:01,330
Definitely.

399
00:19:01,330 --> 00:19:05,770
Sometimes you feel comfortable, but at the same time, you feel like something is missing.

400
00:19:05,770 --> 00:19:08,250
Yes, that feeling is very common.

401
00:19:08,250 --> 00:19:10,710
So let's start from the beginning.

402
00:19:10,710 --> 00:19:13,130
Imagine someone is thinking about changing their job.

403
00:19:13,130 --> 00:19:15,050
What's the first thing they might say?

404
00:19:15,050 --> 00:19:18,930
They might say, I've been thinking about changing my job.

405
00:19:18,930 --> 00:19:20,450
That's a very natural sentence.

406
00:19:20,450 --> 00:19:23,370
You can also say, I'm considering a career change.

407
00:19:23,370 --> 00:19:24,370
Right.

408
00:19:24,370 --> 00:19:28,050
And another useful phrase is, I'm looking for new opportunities.

409
00:19:28,050 --> 00:19:30,930
I like that one because it sounds professional and positive.

410
00:19:30,930 --> 00:19:33,310
doesn't sound negative about your current job.

411
00:19:33,310 --> 00:19:34,310
Exactly.

412
00:19:34,310 --> 00:19:36,790
It's always better to sound positive, especially

413
00:19:36,790 --> 00:19:38,750
in professional conversations.

414
00:19:38,750 --> 00:19:41,710
So if someone asks, why do you want to change your job?

415
00:19:41,710 --> 00:19:43,270
What are some good answers?

416
00:19:43,270 --> 00:19:46,870
One common answer is, I'm looking for new challenges.

417
00:19:46,870 --> 00:19:50,030
Yes, that's a very popular phrase in interviews.

418
00:19:50,030 --> 00:19:53,390
You could also say, I want to develop new skills.

419
00:19:53,390 --> 00:19:55,270
Or I feel like I've learned everything

420
00:19:55,270 --> 00:19:57,070
I can in my current role.

421
00:19:57,070 --> 00:19:58,190
That's a great one.

422
00:19:58,190 --> 00:20:00,990
It shows growth, not dissatisfaction.

423
00:20:00,990 --> 00:20:02,390
Exactly.

424
00:20:02,390 --> 00:20:05,790
Another important phrase is, I'm looking for better career growth.

425
00:20:05,790 --> 00:20:09,670
Yes, and also, I want more responsibility.

426
00:20:09,670 --> 00:20:12,590
Let's talk about a slightly more honest situation.

427
00:20:12,590 --> 00:20:15,110
What if someone is not happy at work?

428
00:20:15,110 --> 00:20:18,830
Then they might say, I feel stuck in my current position.

429
00:20:18,830 --> 00:20:20,630
That's a very natural phrase.

430
00:20:20,630 --> 00:20:22,590
What does feel stuck mean?

431
00:20:22,590 --> 00:20:27,110
It means you feel like you are not progressing or improving, you're in the same place

432
00:20:27,110 --> 00:20:28,750
for too long.

433
00:20:28,750 --> 00:20:30,430
That's very relatable.

434
00:20:30,430 --> 00:20:33,070
Another phrase is, there's no room for growth.

435
00:20:33,070 --> 00:20:36,550
Yes, or I'm not being challenged anymore.

436
00:20:36,550 --> 00:20:38,150
That's a good one for interviews too.

437
00:20:38,150 --> 00:20:40,630
It sounds honest, but still professional.

438
00:20:40,630 --> 00:20:41,950
What about stress?

439
00:20:41,950 --> 00:20:44,830
That's also a reason many people change jobs.

440
00:20:44,830 --> 00:20:45,830
Absolutely.

441
00:20:45,830 --> 00:20:48,870
You can say, I've been under a lot of pressure.

442
00:20:48,870 --> 00:20:50,990
Or I'm feeling burnt out.

443
00:20:50,990 --> 00:20:52,510
That's an important phrase.

444
00:20:52,510 --> 00:20:56,630
Counting out means extremely tired, both mentally and emotionally.

445
00:20:56,630 --> 00:20:57,630
Exactly.

446
00:20:57,630 --> 00:21:00,310
It's stronger than just saying tired.

447
00:21:00,310 --> 00:21:03,110
Let's imagine a conversation between two co-workers.

448
00:21:03,110 --> 00:21:04,750
Okay, I'll start.

449
00:21:04,750 --> 00:21:07,670
Hey, Sophia, can I talk to you about something?

450
00:21:07,670 --> 00:21:08,670
Of course.

451
00:21:08,670 --> 00:21:09,670
What's going on?

452
00:21:09,670 --> 00:21:11,670
I've been thinking about changing my job.

453
00:21:11,670 --> 00:21:12,670
Oh, really?

454
00:21:12,670 --> 00:21:13,830
That's a big decision.

455
00:21:13,830 --> 00:21:15,190
Why are you thinking about it?

456
00:21:15,190 --> 00:21:19,270
I feel like I'm not growing anymore, and I want to try something new.

457
00:21:19,270 --> 00:21:20,270
That makes sense.

458
00:21:20,270 --> 00:21:22,270
already looking for new opportunities?

459
00:21:22,270 --> 00:21:26,270
Yes, I've started updating my resume and applying to a few positions.

460
00:21:26,270 --> 00:21:28,270
That's exciting. How do you feel about it?

461
00:21:28,270 --> 00:21:32,270
Honestly, I'm a bit nervous, but also excited.

462
00:21:32,270 --> 00:21:35,270
That's completely normal. Changing jobs is a big step.

463
00:21:35,270 --> 00:21:40,270
Exactly. I just want to roll where I can learn more and grow professionally.

464
00:21:40,270 --> 00:21:42,270
That sounds like a great goal.

465
00:21:42,270 --> 00:21:45,270
Now let's talk about the next step, job searching.

466
00:21:45,270 --> 00:21:49,270
Yes. Once you decide to change jobs, you start looking for new roles.

467
00:21:49,270 --> 00:21:54,270
You can say, I'm job hunting or I'm applying for new positions.

468
00:21:54,270 --> 00:21:58,270
Another useful phrase is, I'm updating my resume.

469
00:21:58,270 --> 00:22:00,270
And also, I'm writing a cover letter.

470
00:22:00,270 --> 00:22:02,270
Let's explain those quickly.

471
00:22:02,270 --> 00:22:07,270
A resume is a document that shows your experience, skills, and education.

472
00:22:07,270 --> 00:22:12,270
And a cover letter explains why you want the job and why you are a good fit.

473
00:22:12,270 --> 00:22:15,270
Exactly. Now, after applying, what happens?

474
00:22:15,270 --> 00:22:17,270
You wait to hear back.

475
00:22:17,270 --> 00:22:20,770
That's a key phrase. I'm waiting to hear back.

476
00:22:20,770 --> 00:22:23,770
It means you are waiting for a reply from the company.

477
00:22:23,770 --> 00:22:26,270
Then comes the interview stage.

478
00:22:26,270 --> 00:22:29,770
Yes, and that's where communication becomes very important.

479
00:22:29,770 --> 00:22:32,270
Let's practice an interview conversation.

480
00:22:32,270 --> 00:22:33,270
Good idea.

481
00:22:33,270 --> 00:22:36,270
So, Sophia, can you tell me about yourself?

482
00:22:36,270 --> 00:22:41,770
Sure. I have five years of experience in marketing and I specialize in digital campaigns.

483
00:22:41,770 --> 00:22:45,770
I enjoy working in dynamic environments and collaborating with teams.

484
00:22:45,770 --> 00:22:48,270
Why do you want to leave your current job?

485
00:22:48,270 --> 00:22:53,270
I've learned a lot in my current role, but I'm looking for new challenges and opportunities to grow.

486
00:22:53,270 --> 00:22:55,270
That's a perfect answer.

487
00:22:55,270 --> 00:22:57,770
Thank you. What about strengths?

488
00:22:57,770 --> 00:23:00,270
You can say, I'm a strong communicator.

489
00:23:00,270 --> 00:23:02,270
Or I'm a quick learner.

490
00:23:02,270 --> 00:23:04,270
Or I work well under pressure.

491
00:23:04,270 --> 00:23:06,770
Those are all very common and useful.

492
00:23:06,770 --> 00:23:08,770
Now, what about weaknesses?

493
00:23:08,770 --> 00:23:11,270
That's always a tricky question.

494
00:23:11,270 --> 00:23:15,270
Yes, but you can say, sometimes I take on too much work,

495
00:23:15,270 --> 00:23:17,430
but I'm learning to manage my time better.

496
00:23:17,430 --> 00:23:20,270
That shows self-awareness and improvement.

497
00:23:20,270 --> 00:23:23,870
Exactly. Now, after the interview, what do you say?

498
00:23:23,870 --> 00:23:27,070
You might say, I think the interview went well.

499
00:23:27,070 --> 00:23:29,770
Or, I was nervous, but I did my best.

500
00:23:29,770 --> 00:23:31,970
Then, again, you wait.

501
00:23:31,970 --> 00:23:34,770
Yes, and finally, you might get an offer.

502
00:23:34,770 --> 00:23:36,470
That's the best part.

503
00:23:36,470 --> 00:23:39,670
The company might say, we'd like to offer you the position.

504
00:23:39,670 --> 00:23:42,270
You reply, thank you for the offer.

505
00:23:42,270 --> 00:23:44,270
Then comes negotiation.

506
00:23:44,270 --> 00:23:49,070
Yes, very important. You can say, I'd like to discuss the salary.

507
00:23:49,070 --> 00:23:51,770
Or is there any flexibility in the offer?

508
00:23:51,770 --> 00:23:54,070
That sounds polite and professional.

509
00:23:54,070 --> 00:23:58,870
Exactly. Now, let's move to the most difficult part, resigning.

510
00:23:58,870 --> 00:24:01,270
Yes, telling your boss you're leaving.

511
00:24:01,270 --> 00:24:05,070
You can start with, I'd like to talk to you about something important.

512
00:24:05,070 --> 00:24:07,670
Then say, I've decided to move on.

513
00:24:07,670 --> 00:24:09,270
That's a great phrase.

514
00:24:09,270 --> 00:24:12,370
You can also say, I've accepted another position.

515
00:24:12,370 --> 00:24:14,870
And I'd like to give my notice.

516
00:24:14,870 --> 00:24:18,070
Notice means the time before you officially leave.

517
00:24:18,070 --> 00:24:19,870
Usually two weeks.

518
00:24:19,870 --> 00:24:23,370
You can say, my last day will be two weeks from today.

519
00:24:23,370 --> 00:24:25,870
Also, it's important to be polite.

520
00:24:25,870 --> 00:24:28,870
Yes, say, thank you for the opportunity.

521
00:24:28,870 --> 00:24:30,870
And I've learned a lot here.

522
00:24:30,870 --> 00:24:32,870
That helps you leave on good terms.

523
00:24:32,870 --> 00:24:37,370
Exactly. Now, let's imagine the first day at a new job.

524
00:24:37,370 --> 00:24:40,070
That's exciting and scary at the same time.

525
00:24:40,070 --> 00:24:42,270
You can say, nice to meet you.

526
00:24:42,270 --> 00:24:43,930
Or, I'm happy to be here.

527
00:24:43,930 --> 00:24:46,430
Also, could you show me around?

528
00:24:46,430 --> 00:24:48,430
And I'm still learning.

529
00:24:48,430 --> 00:24:50,930
That's one of the most useful phrases.

530
00:24:50,930 --> 00:24:53,230
Yes, very simple and honest.

531
00:24:53,230 --> 00:24:55,430
After a few days, you might say,

532
00:24:55,430 --> 00:24:57,030
I'm getting the hang of it.

533
00:24:57,030 --> 00:25:00,230
That means you are starting to understand and feel comfortable.

534
00:25:00,230 --> 00:25:01,430
Exactly.

535
00:25:01,430 --> 00:25:03,830
This whole journey from thinking about change

536
00:25:03,830 --> 00:25:07,930
to starting a new job requires many small conversations.

537
00:25:07,930 --> 00:25:11,870
And each conversation uses simple but powerful English.

538
00:25:11,870 --> 00:25:16,870
That's the key. You don't need complicated grammar. You need clear and practical phrases.

539
00:25:16,870 --> 00:25:21,870
Let's reflect for a moment. Why do you think people are afraid to change jobs?

540
00:25:21,870 --> 00:25:23,870
I think it's fear of the unknown.

541
00:25:23,870 --> 00:25:26,870
Yes, and also fear of failure.

542
00:25:26,870 --> 00:25:30,870
But at the same time, staying in the wrong job can be worse.

543
00:25:30,870 --> 00:25:35,870
That's true. So, a good phrase is, I want to step out of my comfort zone.

544
00:25:35,870 --> 00:25:37,870
I like that. It shows courage.

545
00:25:37,870 --> 00:25:40,870
Another one is, I'm ready for a new chapter.

546
00:25:40,870 --> 00:25:42,870
That sounds very positive.

547
00:25:42,870 --> 00:25:44,870
Yes, it focuses on the future.

548
00:25:44,870 --> 00:25:48,870
Before we finish, let's recap some key phrases.

549
00:25:48,870 --> 00:25:51,870
Good idea. I'm thinking about changing my job.

550
00:25:51,870 --> 00:25:53,870
I'm looking for new opportunities.

551
00:25:53,870 --> 00:25:55,870
I feel stuck.

552
00:25:55,870 --> 00:25:56,870
I want to grow.

553
00:25:56,870 --> 00:25:58,870
I'm updating my resume.

554
00:25:58,870 --> 00:26:00,870
I'm waiting to hear back.

555
00:26:00,870 --> 00:26:01,870
I got an interview.

556
00:26:01,870 --> 00:26:03,870
I'd like to discuss the salary.

557
00:26:03,870 --> 00:26:05,870
I've decided to move on.

558
00:26:05,870 --> 00:26:07,870
I'm getting the hang of it.

559
00:26:07,870 --> 00:26:14,310
of it. These phrases will help you in real life situations. Absolutely. Now, we want

560
00:26:14,310 --> 00:26:19,950
to hear from you. Yes, this is our favorite part. Our question is, why would you change

561
00:26:19,950 --> 00:26:25,350
your job? You can answer like this. I would change my job because I want better work-life

562
00:26:25,350 --> 00:26:31,950
balance. Or I want to learn new skills. Or I want a higher salary. Write your answer

563
00:26:31,950 --> 00:26:37,070
and practice your English. Don't worry about mistakes. Just try. Thank you so much

564
00:26:37,070 --> 00:26:38,990
for learning with us today.

565
00:26:38,990 --> 00:26:42,670
Keep practicing, keep improving, and keep believing in yourself.

566
00:26:42,670 --> 00:26:44,830
We'll see you in the next lesson.

567
00:26:44,830 --> 00:26:48,970
Take care and goodbye.

568
00:26:48,970 --> 00:26:52,410
Hello everyone and welcome back to Business English Podcast.

569
00:26:52,410 --> 00:26:54,170
We're so happy you're here with us today.

570
00:26:54,170 --> 00:26:55,170
I'm Daniel.

571
00:26:55,170 --> 00:26:56,170
And I'm Sarah.

572
00:26:56,170 --> 00:26:57,530
Thank you for joining us.

573
00:26:57,530 --> 00:27:02,170
Today, we're talking about a topic that is very important for many people, changing

574
00:27:02,170 --> 00:27:05,570
your job and talking about it in business English.

575
00:27:05,570 --> 00:27:06,570
That's right.

576
00:27:06,570 --> 00:27:07,890
Maybe you want a new job.

577
00:27:07,890 --> 00:27:09,970
Maybe you're tired of your current job.

578
00:27:09,970 --> 00:27:14,970
Maybe you want more money, more responsibility, better hours, or simply a fresh start.

579
00:27:14,970 --> 00:27:20,090
Or maybe your boss says, this will only take five minutes, and then suddenly you're still

580
00:27:20,090 --> 00:27:22,090
in the meeting one hour later.

581
00:27:22,090 --> 00:27:23,090
Yes.

582
00:27:23,090 --> 00:27:26,690
And then after the meeting, they send another email with more tasks.

583
00:27:26,690 --> 00:27:27,690
Exactly.

584
00:27:27,690 --> 00:27:32,370
So today we're going to help you learn natural and useful English phrases for talking about

585
00:27:32,370 --> 00:27:33,850
changing jobs.

586
00:27:33,850 --> 00:27:38,450
We'll talk about why people change jobs, how to explain your reasons, how to look for

587
00:27:38,450 --> 00:27:43,570
a new job, how to talk in interviews, and how to leave your old job politely.

588
00:27:43,570 --> 00:27:48,010
We'll also share practical examples and some funny stories, because learning English should

589
00:27:48,010 --> 00:27:50,770
be useful, but it should also be enjoyable.

590
00:27:50,770 --> 00:27:51,770
Absolutely.

591
00:27:51,770 --> 00:27:53,690
So if you're ready, let's get started.

592
00:27:53,690 --> 00:27:56,210
Sarah, have you ever wanted to change your job?

593
00:27:56,210 --> 00:27:57,770
Oh yes, definitely.

594
00:27:57,770 --> 00:28:01,570
I think almost everyone thinks about changing jobs at some point.

595
00:28:01,570 --> 00:28:02,570
Really?

596
00:28:02,570 --> 00:28:03,570
What made you want to change?

597
00:28:03,570 --> 00:28:08,610
Well, a few years ago, I was working in an office where I did exactly the same thing every

598
00:28:08,610 --> 00:28:09,610
day.

599
00:28:09,610 --> 00:28:14,650
I answered emails, updated spreadsheets, printed documents, and attended meetings.

600
00:28:14,650 --> 00:28:15,970
That doesn't sound too bad.

601
00:28:15,970 --> 00:28:20,010
It wasn't terrible, but after two years I started to feel bored.

602
00:28:20,010 --> 00:28:22,370
I felt like I wasn't learning anything new.

603
00:28:22,370 --> 00:28:24,650
Ah, so you felt stuck.

604
00:28:24,650 --> 00:28:25,650
Exactly.

605
00:28:25,650 --> 00:28:27,290
That's a very useful phrase.

606
00:28:27,290 --> 00:28:30,570
You can say, I feel stuck in my current job.

607
00:28:30,570 --> 00:28:33,110
It means you're not growing or moving forward.

608
00:28:33,110 --> 00:28:35,450
I think many people feel that way.

609
00:28:35,450 --> 00:28:38,830
Sometimes you don't hate your job, but you know it's not right for you anymore.

610
00:28:38,830 --> 00:28:39,830
Yes.

611
00:28:39,830 --> 00:28:41,950
Maybe you want more responsibility.

612
00:28:41,950 --> 00:28:44,150
Maybe you want to use different skills.

613
00:28:44,150 --> 00:28:47,710
Or maybe you want a job that matches your interests better.

614
00:28:47,710 --> 00:28:51,030
For example, you could say, I'm looking for a new challenge.

615
00:28:51,030 --> 00:28:52,750
Yes, that's a great phrase.

616
00:28:52,750 --> 00:28:54,990
It sounds positive and professional.

617
00:28:54,990 --> 00:28:58,830
Better than saying, I'm tired of everything and I want to disappear.

618
00:28:58,830 --> 00:28:59,830
Yes.

619
00:28:59,830 --> 00:29:01,370
Definitely better for an interview.

620
00:29:01,370 --> 00:29:04,590
So if someone asks you, why do you want to change your job?

621
00:29:04,590 --> 00:29:05,750
What are some good answers?

622
00:29:05,750 --> 00:29:12,930
You can say, I'm looking for new opportunities, or I want to develop my skills, or I'd like

623
00:29:12,930 --> 00:29:15,270
to work in a different industry.

624
00:29:15,270 --> 00:29:17,190
Industry means the type of business, right?

625
00:29:17,190 --> 00:29:18,190
Exactly.

626
00:29:18,190 --> 00:29:24,430
For example, technology, healthcare, education, marketing, finance, those are all industries.

627
00:29:24,430 --> 00:29:25,430
Good.

628
00:29:25,430 --> 00:29:28,510
You can also say, I want better work-life balance.

629
00:29:28,510 --> 00:29:30,550
That's one of the most common reasons.

630
00:29:30,550 --> 00:29:32,910
What exactly is work-life balance?

631
00:29:32,910 --> 00:29:38,310
It means having enough time for work, but also enough time for your personal life, your family,

632
00:29:38,310 --> 00:29:39,950
your hobbies, and your health.

633
00:29:39,950 --> 00:29:44,670
So if you work 12 hours every day and answer work messages at midnight, you probably do

634
00:29:44,670 --> 00:29:46,910
not have good work-life balance.

635
00:29:46,910 --> 00:29:47,910
Exactly.

636
00:29:47,910 --> 00:29:51,870
You might say, I'm looking for a position with better work-life balance.

637
00:29:51,870 --> 00:29:53,550
That sounds very professional.

638
00:29:53,550 --> 00:29:55,270
Another common reason is salary.

639
00:29:55,270 --> 00:29:56,270
Ah, yes.

640
00:29:56,270 --> 00:29:57,270
Money.

641
00:29:57,270 --> 00:29:58,270
Yes.

642
00:29:58,270 --> 00:30:00,390
Some people change jobs because they want to earn more.

643
00:30:00,390 --> 00:30:03,010
Can you say, I want more money in an interview?

644
00:30:03,010 --> 00:30:05,990
You can, but it's better to say it more professionally.

645
00:30:05,990 --> 00:30:10,590
For example, I'm looking for a position with better compensation.

646
00:30:10,590 --> 00:30:12,630
Compensation means salary and benefits.

647
00:30:12,630 --> 00:30:13,630
Exactly.

648
00:30:13,630 --> 00:30:18,270
Or you can say, I believe my skills and experience are worth a higher salary.

649
00:30:18,270 --> 00:30:19,270
Nice.

650
00:30:19,270 --> 00:30:20,370
That sounds confident.

651
00:30:20,370 --> 00:30:23,730
Another reason is that some people are simply burned out.

652
00:30:23,730 --> 00:30:26,110
Burned out is a very useful phrase.

653
00:30:26,110 --> 00:30:27,110
Yes.

654
00:30:27,110 --> 00:30:30,510
burnout means extremely tired and stressed because of work.

655
00:30:30,510 --> 00:30:35,710
So if someone works every weekend, answers emails all night and never takes a vacation,

656
00:30:35,710 --> 00:30:37,310
they might feel burned out.

657
00:30:37,310 --> 00:30:38,310
Exactly.

658
00:30:38,310 --> 00:30:42,710
They might say, I've been under a lot of pressure and I need a healthier schedule.

659
00:30:42,710 --> 00:30:45,030
That sounds honest but not too negative.

660
00:30:45,030 --> 00:30:46,030
Right.

661
00:30:46,030 --> 00:30:49,070
It's important to stay positive when talking about changing jobs.

662
00:30:49,070 --> 00:30:50,070
Why?

663
00:30:50,070 --> 00:30:54,110
Because if you complain too much about your old job, people may think you are difficult

664
00:30:54,110 --> 00:30:55,110
to work with.

665
00:30:55,110 --> 00:30:56,110
That's true.

666
00:30:56,110 --> 00:30:59,430
Even if your old boss was terrible, you should still speak politely.

667
00:30:59,430 --> 00:31:00,430
Exactly.

668
00:31:00,430 --> 00:31:05,590
Instead of saying, my boss was awful, you can say, I'm looking for a different management

669
00:31:05,590 --> 00:31:06,590
style.

670
00:31:06,590 --> 00:31:07,590
That is a much safer answer.

671
00:31:07,590 --> 00:31:08,590
Yes.

672
00:31:08,590 --> 00:31:13,470
Or if your company had no opportunities for promotion, you can say, there wasn't much

673
00:31:13,470 --> 00:31:15,670
room for growth in my current role.

674
00:31:15,670 --> 00:31:17,870
I like that phrase, room for growth.

675
00:31:17,870 --> 00:31:18,870
Me too.

676
00:31:18,870 --> 00:31:23,030
It means the chance to learn, improve, or move to a higher position.

677
00:31:23,030 --> 00:31:28,010
So if you stay in the same position for five years and nothing changes, you might say there's

678
00:31:28,010 --> 00:31:30,390
no room for growth in my current role.

679
00:31:30,390 --> 00:31:31,390
Exactly.

680
00:31:31,390 --> 00:31:33,670
Okay, so you decide you want a new job.

681
00:31:33,670 --> 00:31:34,710
What's the first step?

682
00:31:34,710 --> 00:31:36,910
The first step is to update your resume.

683
00:31:36,910 --> 00:31:37,910
Ah, yes.

684
00:31:37,910 --> 00:31:38,910
The famous resume.

685
00:31:38,910 --> 00:31:44,950
A resume is a document that shows your work experience, education, skills, and achievements.

686
00:31:44,950 --> 00:31:50,150
I always think updating a resume is difficult because you have to make yourself sound impressive.

687
00:31:50,150 --> 00:31:51,470
That's true.

688
00:31:51,470 --> 00:31:53,970
people write, I answered the phone.

689
00:31:53,970 --> 00:31:59,470
But on a resume, you write managed communication with clients and handled incoming inquiries.

690
00:31:59,470 --> 00:32:00,470
Exactly.

691
00:32:00,470 --> 00:32:02,290
It sounds much more professional.

692
00:32:02,290 --> 00:32:06,010
So if I want to change jobs, I can say I'm updating my resume.

693
00:32:06,010 --> 00:32:07,010
Yes.

694
00:32:07,010 --> 00:32:09,310
And you may also need to write a cover letter.

695
00:32:09,310 --> 00:32:11,530
Cover letters are always difficult for me.

696
00:32:11,530 --> 00:32:12,910
Many people feel that way.

697
00:32:12,910 --> 00:32:17,250
But a cover letter is simply a short letter that explains why you want the job and

698
00:32:17,250 --> 00:32:18,970
why you are a good fit.

699
00:32:18,970 --> 00:32:21,050
Good fit is another useful phrase.

700
00:32:21,050 --> 00:32:25,130
Yes, you can say, I think I'm a good fit for this position.

701
00:32:25,130 --> 00:32:26,130
Then what?

702
00:32:26,130 --> 00:32:27,690
Then you start applying for jobs.

703
00:32:27,690 --> 00:32:30,410
So you can say, I'm applying for several positions.

704
00:32:30,410 --> 00:32:31,410
Exactly.

705
00:32:31,410 --> 00:32:34,610
Or you can say, I've sent out ten applications this week.

706
00:32:34,610 --> 00:32:35,610
Ten?

707
00:32:35,610 --> 00:32:36,610
That's a lot.

708
00:32:36,610 --> 00:32:38,410
Yes, job searching can take time.

709
00:32:38,410 --> 00:32:41,410
You can also say, I'm looking at job postings online.

710
00:32:41,410 --> 00:32:44,770
Yes, a job posting is an advertisement for a job.

711
00:32:44,770 --> 00:32:47,170
Where do people usually look for job postings?

712
00:32:47,170 --> 00:32:52,210
websites like LinkedIn, Indeed, Company websites, or even social media.

713
00:32:52,210 --> 00:32:56,050
I have a friend who checks job websites every morning before breakfast.

714
00:32:56,050 --> 00:32:57,370
That's very organized.

715
00:32:57,370 --> 00:33:01,410
Yes, but sometimes he gets so excited that he forgets to eat breakfast.

716
00:33:01,410 --> 00:33:02,410
That is not good.

717
00:33:02,410 --> 00:33:04,410
You need breakfast and a job.

718
00:33:04,410 --> 00:33:05,410
True.

719
00:33:05,410 --> 00:33:08,370
The other useful phrase is, I'm waiting to hear back.

720
00:33:08,370 --> 00:33:10,530
Hear back means receive an answer.

721
00:33:10,530 --> 00:33:11,530
Exactly.

722
00:33:11,530 --> 00:33:16,050
For example, I applied for the job last week and now I'm waiting to hear back.

723
00:33:16,050 --> 00:33:17,850
Being is always the hardest part.

724
00:33:17,850 --> 00:33:20,690
Yes, you check your email every five minutes.

725
00:33:20,690 --> 00:33:23,490
And then the email is only a supermarket advertisement.

726
00:33:23,490 --> 00:33:24,490
Exactly.

727
00:33:24,490 --> 00:33:26,690
But eventually, maybe you get an interview.

728
00:33:26,690 --> 00:33:29,250
Yes, and then it's time to prepare.

729
00:33:29,250 --> 00:33:30,850
Interviews can be very stressful.

730
00:33:30,850 --> 00:33:33,090
They can, but preparation helps.

731
00:33:33,090 --> 00:33:35,410
What are some common interview questions?

732
00:33:35,410 --> 00:33:38,290
The first question is often, can you tell me about yourself?

733
00:33:38,290 --> 00:33:40,250
I never know how to answer that.

734
00:33:40,250 --> 00:33:41,250
Many people don't.

735
00:33:41,250 --> 00:33:43,530
But the answer should be simple and professional.

736
00:33:43,530 --> 00:33:44,730
Can you give an example?

737
00:33:44,730 --> 00:33:45,730
Sure.

738
00:33:45,730 --> 00:33:50,910
say, I've worked in customer service for four years. In my current job, I help customers

739
00:33:50,910 --> 00:33:55,410
solve problems and manage daily reports. Now I'm looking for a new opportunity where

740
00:33:55,410 --> 00:34:00,290
I can grow and take on more responsibility. That sounds great. Thank you. Another common

741
00:34:00,290 --> 00:34:05,570
question is, why do you want this job? Yes, you can answer, I'm interested in this

742
00:34:05,570 --> 00:34:10,370
role because it matches my experience and skills. Or, I've always wanted to work

743
00:34:10,370 --> 00:34:14,850
in this industry. Exactly. What about the question, why do you want to leave

744
00:34:14,850 --> 00:34:16,290
your current job.

745
00:34:16,290 --> 00:34:17,370
That's very important.

746
00:34:17,370 --> 00:34:19,410
You should never be too negative.

747
00:34:19,410 --> 00:34:22,890
So don't say because my boss is crazy.

748
00:34:22,890 --> 00:34:23,890
Definitely not.

749
00:34:23,890 --> 00:34:25,330
Okay, then what should you say?

750
00:34:25,330 --> 00:34:29,930
You can say, I've learned a lot in my current position, but I'm ready for a new challenge.

751
00:34:29,930 --> 00:34:30,930
Nice.

752
00:34:30,930 --> 00:34:34,110
Or, I'm looking for more opportunities to develop my skills.

753
00:34:34,110 --> 00:34:35,490
That sounds much better.

754
00:34:35,490 --> 00:34:38,090
Yes, it keeps the conversation positive.

755
00:34:38,090 --> 00:34:40,330
What if they ask about your strengths?

756
00:34:40,330 --> 00:34:44,690
Then you can say things like, I'm organized, I'm a quick learner, I communicate

757
00:34:44,690 --> 00:34:46,690
I work well under pressure.

758
00:34:46,690 --> 00:34:49,690
I think I'm a quick learner is very useful.

759
00:34:49,690 --> 00:34:52,690
Yes, especially if you are changing to a new industry.

760
00:34:52,690 --> 00:34:55,690
Can I say I'm very good at solving problems?

761
00:34:55,690 --> 00:34:57,690
Absolutely. What about weaknesses?

762
00:34:57,690 --> 00:35:00,690
Ah yes, everyone's favorite question.

763
00:35:00,690 --> 00:35:01,690
I hate that question.

764
00:35:01,690 --> 00:35:04,690
Most people do, but you should choose a real weakness

765
00:35:04,690 --> 00:35:06,690
and explain how you're improving.

766
00:35:06,690 --> 00:35:07,690
For example?

767
00:35:07,690 --> 00:35:10,690
Sometimes I spend too much time checking details

768
00:35:10,690 --> 00:35:12,690
because I want everything to be perfect,

769
00:35:12,690 --> 00:35:14,890
but I'm learning to manage my time better.

770
00:35:14,890 --> 00:35:15,690
That's good.

771
00:35:15,690 --> 00:35:16,890
Or you can say,

772
00:35:16,890 --> 00:35:19,590
I used to feel nervous speaking in front of groups,

773
00:35:19,590 --> 00:35:22,290
but I've been practicing and now I'm more confident.

774
00:35:22,290 --> 00:35:23,590
Much better than saying,

775
00:35:23,590 --> 00:35:25,590
my weakness is that I'm always right.

776
00:35:25,590 --> 00:35:27,690
Yes, please do not say that.

777
00:35:27,690 --> 00:35:29,490
After the interview, what can you say?

778
00:35:29,490 --> 00:35:30,390
You can say,

779
00:35:30,390 --> 00:35:32,090
I think the interview went well.

780
00:35:32,090 --> 00:35:34,790
Or I was nervous at first, but then I relaxed.

781
00:35:34,790 --> 00:35:35,590
Yes.

782
00:35:35,590 --> 00:35:37,690
Or I hope they offer me the job.

783
00:35:37,690 --> 00:35:39,090
Then you wait again.

784
00:35:39,090 --> 00:35:40,190
More waiting.

785
00:35:40,190 --> 00:35:42,490
And finally, maybe you get an offer.

786
00:35:42,490 --> 00:35:46,490
Yes. Then the company says, we'd like to offer you the position.

787
00:35:46,490 --> 00:35:48,150
That must feel amazing.

788
00:35:48,150 --> 00:35:48,990
It does.

789
00:35:48,990 --> 00:35:50,150
So what do you say?

790
00:35:50,150 --> 00:35:52,950
First, you say, thank you very much for the offer.

791
00:35:52,950 --> 00:35:54,350
Then can you ask questions?

792
00:35:54,350 --> 00:36:00,750
Of course. You should ask about salary, benefits, working hours, remote work, and vacation.

793
00:36:00,750 --> 00:36:03,290
For example, what is the salary range?

794
00:36:03,290 --> 00:36:07,290
Exactly. Or does the company offer flexible working hours?

795
00:36:07,290 --> 00:36:11,350
Benefits, again, are extra things you receive in addition to your salary,

796
00:36:11,350 --> 00:36:15,750
like health insurance, paid vacation, retirement plans, and training.

797
00:36:15,750 --> 00:36:16,750
Can you negotiate?

798
00:36:16,750 --> 00:36:17,750
Yes.

799
00:36:17,750 --> 00:36:18,870
Negotiating is normal.

800
00:36:18,870 --> 00:36:20,550
How do you do that politely?

801
00:36:20,550 --> 00:36:23,990
You can say, I was hoping for a slightly higher salary.

802
00:36:23,990 --> 00:36:24,990
That sounds polite.

803
00:36:24,990 --> 00:36:28,470
Or, based on my experience, I'd like to discuss the offer.

804
00:36:28,470 --> 00:36:29,470
Nice.

805
00:36:29,470 --> 00:36:33,070
Another useful phrase is, is there any flexibility in the salary?

806
00:36:33,070 --> 00:36:34,070
Very professional.

807
00:36:34,070 --> 00:36:35,890
Then maybe you accept the offer.

808
00:36:35,890 --> 00:36:38,830
You can say, I'd be happy to accept the position.

809
00:36:38,830 --> 00:36:41,070
Or I'm pleased to accept your offer.

810
00:36:41,070 --> 00:36:43,570
But then comes the difficult part.

811
00:36:43,570 --> 00:36:44,870
Telling your current boss.

812
00:36:44,870 --> 00:36:45,870
Exactly.

813
00:36:45,870 --> 00:36:48,570
I think many people are afraid of that conversation.

814
00:36:48,570 --> 00:36:52,570
Yes, because they worry that their boss will be angry or disappointed.

815
00:36:52,570 --> 00:36:54,070
So what should you say?

816
00:36:54,070 --> 00:36:56,270
First, ask for a private meeting.

817
00:36:56,270 --> 00:36:58,770
You can say, do you have a few minutes to talk?

818
00:36:58,770 --> 00:36:59,770
Exactly.

819
00:36:59,770 --> 00:37:02,170
Then you can say, I've decided to move on.

820
00:37:02,170 --> 00:37:04,370
Move on is a very useful phrase.

821
00:37:04,370 --> 00:37:07,770
Yes, it means you are leaving for a new opportunity.

822
00:37:07,770 --> 00:37:10,370
Then you can say, I've accepted another position.

823
00:37:10,370 --> 00:37:13,170
Or you can say, I'd like to give my notice.

824
00:37:13,170 --> 00:37:15,690
Notice means telling the company that you were leaving.

825
00:37:15,690 --> 00:37:16,690
Right.

826
00:37:16,690 --> 00:37:18,810
Usually people give two weeks notice.

827
00:37:18,810 --> 00:37:22,210
So you can say, my last day will be two weeks from today.

828
00:37:22,210 --> 00:37:23,210
Exactly.

829
00:37:23,210 --> 00:37:24,210
Should you thank your boss?

830
00:37:24,210 --> 00:37:25,210
Definitely.

831
00:37:25,210 --> 00:37:28,630
Even if the job wasn't perfect, it's important to leave professionally.

832
00:37:28,630 --> 00:37:30,850
You can say, thank you for the opportunity.

833
00:37:30,850 --> 00:37:33,610
Or you can say, I've learned a lot working here.

834
00:37:33,610 --> 00:37:35,250
I think that's very important.

835
00:37:35,250 --> 00:37:36,250
Yes.

836
00:37:36,250 --> 00:37:39,170
Because you never know when you may work with those people again.

837
00:37:39,170 --> 00:37:40,170
That's true.

838
00:37:40,170 --> 00:37:44,250
world can be surprisingly small. Exactly. You should leave on good…

839
00:37:44,250 --> 00:37:48,050
Hello and welcome back to Business English Podcast.

840
00:37:48,050 --> 00:37:52,010
Hi everyone. Welcome to today's English Conversation Practice.

841
00:37:52,010 --> 00:37:55,570
I'm Leo and we're really happy you're here with us today.

842
00:37:55,570 --> 00:38:00,090
And I'm Tina. On this channel, we help you speak English more naturally through real

843
00:38:00,090 --> 00:38:05,130
conversations, practical examples, and useful phrases you can use at work.

844
00:38:05,130 --> 00:38:10,690
Our goal is to make English simple, clear, and something you can actually use in real

845
00:38:10,690 --> 00:38:11,690
life.

846
00:38:11,690 --> 00:38:12,690
Exactly.

847
00:38:12,690 --> 00:38:16,130
Not just theory, but real workplace communication.

848
00:38:16,130 --> 00:38:19,850
Today's topic is very important and very practical.

849
00:38:19,850 --> 00:38:24,410
We're talking about how to talk about changing your job in business English.

850
00:38:24,410 --> 00:38:29,690
Yes, and this is something almost everyone experiences at some point in their career.

851
00:38:29,690 --> 00:38:31,250
Maybe you feel stuck.

852
00:38:31,250 --> 00:38:33,250
Maybe you want a higher salary.

853
00:38:33,250 --> 00:38:36,090
Maybe you want better work-life balance.

854
00:38:36,090 --> 00:38:39,490
Or maybe you just want a fresh start and a new environment.

855
00:38:39,490 --> 00:38:45,250
And the challenge is not just changing jobs, it's talking about it clearly and professionally

856
00:38:45,250 --> 00:38:46,250
in English.

857
00:38:46,250 --> 00:38:47,250
Exactly.

858
00:38:47,250 --> 00:38:51,650
You need to explain your reasons, your goals, your experience, and your decisions

859
00:38:51,650 --> 00:38:54,050
in a confident and natural way.

860
00:38:54,050 --> 00:38:58,770
So today, we're going to walk through the entire journey, from thinking about changing

861
00:38:58,770 --> 00:39:01,170
your job to starting a new one.

862
00:39:01,170 --> 00:39:05,010
It will include lots of practical phrases and real-life examples.

863
00:39:05,010 --> 00:39:06,450
Alright, Tina.

864
00:39:06,450 --> 00:39:07,530
Let's start simple.

865
00:39:07,530 --> 00:39:08,530
How are you today?

866
00:39:08,530 --> 00:39:10,090
I'm doing well, thank you.

867
00:39:10,090 --> 00:39:11,930
A bit busy, but in a good way.

868
00:39:11,930 --> 00:39:13,650
I had a productive morning.

869
00:39:13,650 --> 00:39:14,650
That sounds nice.

870
00:39:14,650 --> 00:39:15,650
What did you do?

871
00:39:15,650 --> 00:39:20,570
I reviewed some reports, answered emails, and planned my tasks for the week.

872
00:39:20,570 --> 00:39:21,570
Very organized.

873
00:39:21,570 --> 00:39:22,570
I try.

874
00:39:22,570 --> 00:39:23,570
What about you?

875
00:39:23,570 --> 00:39:27,650
I'm okay, but I've been thinking a lot about my job lately.

876
00:39:27,650 --> 00:39:28,810
Oh, really?

877
00:39:28,810 --> 00:39:30,050
That sounds serious.

878
00:39:30,050 --> 00:39:31,050
What's on your mind?

879
00:39:31,050 --> 00:39:34,170
Well, I've been thinking about changing my job.

880
00:39:34,170 --> 00:39:38,010
That is a big decision. How long have you been thinking about it?

881
00:39:38,010 --> 00:39:43,690
For a few months now. At first it was just a small thought, but now it's becoming more serious.

882
00:39:43,690 --> 00:39:47,610
That's very common. Sometimes the idea grows slowly.

883
00:39:47,610 --> 00:39:51,930
Yes, exactly. At first I thought maybe I just need a vacation.

884
00:39:51,930 --> 00:39:53,930
That's always the first solution.

885
00:39:53,930 --> 00:39:56,970
But even after resting I still feel the same.

886
00:39:56,970 --> 00:40:00,090
So how would you describe your feeling in English?

887
00:40:00,090 --> 00:40:03,370
I would say, I feel stuck in my current role.

888
00:40:03,370 --> 00:40:06,650
That's a very useful phrase. I feel stuck.

889
00:40:06,650 --> 00:40:12,330
Yes, I've been doing the same tasks for a long time, and I don't feel challenged anymore.

890
00:40:12,330 --> 00:40:16,330
Another excellent phrase. I don't feel challenged anymore.

891
00:40:16,330 --> 00:40:19,610
I want to grow professionally and learn new skills.

892
00:40:19,610 --> 00:40:23,290
So you can say, I'm looking for opportunities to grow.

893
00:40:23,290 --> 00:40:27,770
Exactly. That sounds much more professional than just saying I'm bored.

894
00:40:27,770 --> 00:40:33,930
Yes, because I'm bored sounds negative, but I'm looking for growth sounds positive.

895
00:40:33,930 --> 00:40:35,170
That's a key point.

896
00:40:35,170 --> 00:40:39,450
When talking about changing jobs, always try to sound positive.

897
00:40:39,450 --> 00:40:40,730
Absolutely.

898
00:40:40,730 --> 00:40:44,850
Even if your experience is negative, your language should be professional.

899
00:40:44,850 --> 00:40:47,850
Let's talk about more reasons people change jobs.

900
00:40:47,850 --> 00:40:48,850
Sure.

901
00:40:48,850 --> 00:40:51,250
Salary is one of the most common reasons.

902
00:40:51,250 --> 00:40:52,250
Right.

903
00:40:52,250 --> 00:40:54,930
You can say, I'm looking for a higher salary.

904
00:40:54,930 --> 00:40:57,650
Or I'd like better compensation.

905
00:40:57,650 --> 00:41:04,050
sounds very professional. Yes, compensation includes salary and benefits. Another reason

906
00:41:04,050 --> 00:41:09,590
is work-life balance. Very important. You can say, I'm looking for better work-life

907
00:41:09,590 --> 00:41:15,730
balance. Or I want a healthier work schedule. That's a great phrase. Some people also

908
00:41:15,730 --> 00:41:21,970
say my workload is too heavy. Or I've been under a lot of pressure. What about career

909
00:41:21,970 --> 00:41:27,530
growth? Yes, you can say there's no room for growth in my current position. That's

910
00:41:27,530 --> 00:41:29,890
very clear and professional.

911
00:41:29,890 --> 00:41:33,590
Or you can say, I'm looking for more responsibility.

912
00:41:33,590 --> 00:41:37,090
Let's add one more reason, company culture.

913
00:41:37,090 --> 00:41:38,090
Good point.

914
00:41:38,090 --> 00:41:41,490
You can say, I'm looking for a better cultural fit.

915
00:41:41,490 --> 00:41:43,490
That's advanced but very useful.

916
00:41:43,490 --> 00:41:47,770
Yes, it means you want to work in an environment that matches your values.

917
00:41:47,770 --> 00:41:50,330
Now, let's move to the next stage.

918
00:41:50,330 --> 00:41:53,030
You've decided to explore new opportunities.

919
00:41:53,030 --> 00:41:54,130
What do you say?

920
00:41:54,130 --> 00:41:57,410
You can say, I'm currently looking for a new position.

921
00:41:57,410 --> 00:42:00,010
or I'm exploring new opportunities.

922
00:42:00,010 --> 00:42:01,290
I like exploring.

923
00:42:01,290 --> 00:42:03,450
It sounds relaxed and open.

924
00:42:03,450 --> 00:42:05,670
Yes, it doesn't sound desperate.

925
00:42:05,670 --> 00:42:08,130
Then you prepare your documents.

926
00:42:08,130 --> 00:42:10,730
Right, I'm updating my resume.

927
00:42:10,730 --> 00:42:14,090
And I'm writing or improving my cover letter.

928
00:42:14,090 --> 00:42:16,050
After that, you start applying.

929
00:42:16,050 --> 00:42:19,530
You can say, I applied for several jobs this week.

930
00:42:19,530 --> 00:42:22,330
Or I've sent out multiple applications.

931
00:42:22,330 --> 00:42:24,650
Then comes the waiting period.

932
00:42:24,650 --> 00:42:28,650
Yes, and you can say, I'm waiting to hear back from employers.

933
00:42:28,650 --> 00:42:30,650
That's a very natural phrase.

934
00:42:30,650 --> 00:42:33,250
Now, let's imagine you get an interview.

935
00:42:33,250 --> 00:42:36,350
That's exciting and stressful at the same time.

936
00:42:36,350 --> 00:42:39,150
You can say, I've been invited for an interview.

937
00:42:39,150 --> 00:42:42,250
Or I have an interview scheduled for next week.

938
00:42:42,250 --> 00:42:44,150
Then you prepare your answers.

939
00:42:44,150 --> 00:42:45,550
Let's practice some.

940
00:42:45,550 --> 00:42:49,050
Question, why do you want to leave your current job?

941
00:42:49,050 --> 00:42:53,450
Answer, I'm looking for new challenges and opportunities to grow.

942
00:42:53,450 --> 00:42:57,450
Another answer, I want to develop my skills in a new environment.

943
00:42:57,450 --> 00:43:01,450
Or I'm seeking a role that better aligns with my career goals.

944
00:43:01,450 --> 00:43:02,950
That's excellent.

945
00:43:02,950 --> 00:43:05,450
Next question, what are your strengths?

946
00:43:05,450 --> 00:43:08,450
You can say, I'm a strong communicator.

947
00:43:08,450 --> 00:43:11,950
Or I'm highly organized and detail-oriented.

948
00:43:11,950 --> 00:43:14,450
Another one, I work well under pressure.

949
00:43:14,450 --> 00:43:16,950
Very useful in many jobs.

950
00:43:16,950 --> 00:43:18,450
Now, weaknesses.

951
00:43:18,450 --> 00:43:24,450
You can say, I sometimes take on too many tasks, but I'm learning to prioritize better.

952
00:43:24,450 --> 00:43:26,450
That shows growth and awareness.

953
00:43:26,450 --> 00:43:29,450
Now, after the interview, what do you say?

954
00:43:29,450 --> 00:43:31,450
I think the interview went well.

955
00:43:31,450 --> 00:43:34,450
Or I felt confident about my answers.

956
00:43:34,450 --> 00:43:35,450
Then you wait again.

957
00:43:35,450 --> 00:43:38,450
Yes, I'm waiting for their decision.

958
00:43:38,450 --> 00:43:40,450
Now comes the offer stage.

959
00:43:40,450 --> 00:43:42,450
The most exciting part.

960
00:43:42,450 --> 00:43:45,450
The company says we'd like to offer you the position.

961
00:43:45,450 --> 00:43:49,210
And you respond, thank you for the offer.

962
00:43:49,210 --> 00:43:50,610
Then you ask questions.

963
00:43:50,610 --> 00:43:51,610
Check.

964
00:43:51,610 --> 00:43:53,450
What is the salary range?

965
00:43:53,450 --> 00:43:55,210
What benefits are included?

966
00:43:55,210 --> 00:43:57,970
Is there flexibility in working hours?

967
00:43:57,970 --> 00:43:59,810
Is remote work available?

968
00:43:59,810 --> 00:44:02,050
Now let's talk about negotiation.

969
00:44:02,050 --> 00:44:04,290
Yes, very important.

970
00:44:04,290 --> 00:44:07,610
You can say, I'd like to discuss the salary.

971
00:44:07,610 --> 00:44:12,330
Or based on my experience, I was expecting a slightly higher offer.

972
00:44:12,330 --> 00:44:14,330
That's polite and professional.

973
00:44:14,330 --> 00:44:17,370
Yes, negotiation doesn't have to be aggressive.

974
00:44:17,370 --> 00:44:19,650
After that, you make a decision.

975
00:44:19,650 --> 00:44:22,570
You can say, I'd be happy to accept the offer.

976
00:44:22,570 --> 00:44:25,650
Or I've decided to accept the position.

977
00:44:25,650 --> 00:44:27,890
If you refuse, you say, thank you,

978
00:44:27,890 --> 00:44:30,010
but I've decided to decline.

979
00:44:30,010 --> 00:44:31,330
Very polite.

980
00:44:31,330 --> 00:44:34,890
Now comes the difficult conversation, resigning.

981
00:44:34,890 --> 00:44:37,930
Yes, many people feel nervous about this.

982
00:44:37,930 --> 00:44:41,650
You can start with, I'd like to discuss something important.

983
00:44:41,650 --> 00:44:44,930
Then, say, I've decided to move on.

984
00:44:44,930 --> 00:44:47,610
Or I've accepted another opportunity.

985
00:44:47,610 --> 00:44:50,210
And I'd like to give my notice.

986
00:44:50,210 --> 00:44:52,370
Then specify your last day.

987
00:44:52,370 --> 00:44:54,770
My last working day will be.

988
00:44:54,770 --> 00:44:57,010
It's important to stay respectful.

989
00:44:57,010 --> 00:44:59,730
Yes, thank you for the opportunity.

990
00:44:59,730 --> 00:45:02,050
I've learned a lot during my time here.

991
00:45:02,050 --> 00:45:04,090
I appreciate your support.

992
00:45:04,090 --> 00:45:06,290
You can also say, I'll do my best

993
00:45:06,290 --> 00:45:08,610
to ensure a smooth transition.

994
00:45:08,610 --> 00:45:10,330
That's very professional.

995
00:45:10,330 --> 00:45:12,970
Now, let's move to your new job.

996
00:45:12,970 --> 00:45:14,450
The fresh start.

997
00:45:14,450 --> 00:45:17,610
On your first day, you can say, nice to meet you.

998
00:45:17,610 --> 00:45:19,870
And I'm excited to be here.

999
00:45:19,870 --> 00:45:22,570
You can ask, could you show me how this works?

1000
00:45:22,570 --> 00:45:25,290
Or who should I ask if I need help?

1001
00:45:25,290 --> 00:45:28,650
If you don't understand something, I'm still learning.

1002
00:45:28,650 --> 00:45:31,010
Or could you explain that again?

1003
00:45:31,010 --> 00:45:32,890
After a few days, you can say,

1004
00:45:32,890 --> 00:45:35,050
I'm starting to feel more comfortable.

1005
00:45:35,050 --> 00:45:37,130
Or I'm getting the hang of it.

1006
00:45:37,130 --> 00:45:38,870
That means you're improving.

1007
00:45:38,870 --> 00:45:43,510
So, Tina, what's the most important advice for someone changing jobs?

1008
00:45:43,510 --> 00:45:47,830
I would say be clear, be positive, and be professional.

1009
00:45:47,830 --> 00:45:50,790
I agree, and take it one step at a time.

1010
00:45:50,790 --> 00:45:53,270
Yes, don't rush the process.

1011
00:45:53,270 --> 00:45:55,510
Changing jobs can feel scary.

1012
00:45:55,510 --> 00:45:58,070
But it can also be a great opportunity.

1013
00:45:58,070 --> 00:46:00,150
So don't be afraid to try.

1014
00:46:00,150 --> 00:46:02,390
And don't be afraid to speak.

1015
00:46:02,390 --> 00:46:04,070
Practice these phrases.

1016
00:46:04,070 --> 00:46:06,390
Use them in real situations.

1017
00:46:06,390 --> 00:46:08,470
Now we want to hear from you.

1018
00:46:08,470 --> 00:46:11,070
Yes, this is your turn to practice.

1019
00:46:11,070 --> 00:46:14,590
Our question is, why would you change your job?

1020
00:46:14,590 --> 00:46:17,750
You can say, I would change my job because...

1021
00:46:17,750 --> 00:46:19,590
Or, I'm looking for...

1022
00:46:19,590 --> 00:46:21,430
Keep it simple and clear.

1023
00:46:21,430 --> 00:46:24,110
Thank you so much for learning with us today.

1024
00:46:24,110 --> 00:46:26,150
We hope this conversation helps you speak

1025
00:46:26,150 --> 00:46:28,070
more confidently at work.

1026
00:46:28,070 --> 00:46:30,150
Keep practicing every day.

1027
00:46:30,150 --> 00:46:34,710
And remember, small phrases can help you express big ideas.

1028
00:46:34,710 --> 00:46:36,070
Have a wonderful day.

1029
00:46:36,070 --> 00:46:37,150
Goodbye, everyone.

1030
00:46:37,150 --> 00:46:40,670
Hello, and welcome back to Business English Podcast.

1031
00:46:40,670 --> 00:46:41,630
Hi, everyone.

1032
00:46:41,630 --> 00:46:45,030
Welcome to today's English Conversation Practice.

1033
00:46:45,030 --> 00:46:45,990
I'm Daniel.

1034
00:46:45,990 --> 00:46:48,470
And I'm Sophia, and we're really happy

1035
00:46:48,470 --> 00:46:50,190
you're here learning with us today.

1036
00:46:50,190 --> 00:46:53,190
As always, we're here to help you speak English naturally,

1037
00:46:53,190 --> 00:46:55,070
confidently, and effectively

1038
00:46:55,070 --> 00:46:57,110
in real workplace situations.

1039
00:46:57,110 --> 00:46:58,050
That's right.

1040
00:46:58,050 --> 00:47:01,310
Our goal is to make English simple, practical,

1041
00:47:01,310 --> 00:47:04,850
and useful for your daily life, especially at work.

1042
00:47:04,850 --> 00:47:10,210
And today's topic is very important for professionals, employees, and even students who are planning

1043
00:47:10,210 --> 00:47:11,810
their future careers.

1044
00:47:11,810 --> 00:47:15,050
We're going to talk about changing your job in business English.

1045
00:47:15,050 --> 00:47:19,570
Yes, this is something almost everyone experiences at some point.

1046
00:47:19,570 --> 00:47:24,930
Maybe you feel stuck, maybe you want better opportunities, or maybe you just want a fresh

1047
00:47:24,930 --> 00:47:25,930
start.

1048
00:47:25,930 --> 00:47:26,930
Exactly.

1049
00:47:26,930 --> 00:47:31,050
And the key is not just deciding to change your job, but being able to talk about

1050
00:47:31,050 --> 00:47:33,730
it clearly and professionally in English.

1051
00:47:33,730 --> 00:47:38,390
In today's conversation, we'll guide you through everything, from thinking about leaving

1052
00:47:38,390 --> 00:47:44,830
your job, to job searching, interviews, resignation, and starting a new role.

1053
00:47:44,830 --> 00:47:49,210
And we'll use natural conversations, real examples, and practical phrases that you

1054
00:47:49,210 --> 00:47:50,610
can actually use.

1055
00:47:50,610 --> 00:47:55,370
So if you're ready to improve your business English and talk about career changes with

1056
00:47:55,370 --> 00:47:57,770
confidence, let's get started.

1057
00:47:57,770 --> 00:48:00,250
So Sophia, let me ask you something.

1058
00:48:00,250 --> 00:48:03,410
Have you ever seriously thought about changing your job?

1059
00:48:03,410 --> 00:48:05,410
Oh yes, definitely.

1060
00:48:05,410 --> 00:48:09,370
I think almost everyone reaches that point at some stage in their career.

1061
00:48:09,370 --> 00:48:10,810
What made you feel that way?

1062
00:48:10,810 --> 00:48:13,290
Well, for me, it was a combination of things.

1063
00:48:13,290 --> 00:48:18,690
I felt like I wasn't learning anything new, and my daily tasks became very repetitive.

1064
00:48:18,690 --> 00:48:20,530
That's a very common reason.

1065
00:48:20,530 --> 00:48:23,730
So you could say, I felt stuck in my role.

1066
00:48:23,730 --> 00:48:24,730
Exactly.

1067
00:48:24,730 --> 00:48:25,730
That's a perfect phrase.

1068
00:48:25,730 --> 00:48:29,490
I felt stuck, and I also wanted to grow professionally.

1069
00:48:29,490 --> 00:48:31,630
Growth is a big reason for change.

1070
00:48:31,630 --> 00:48:36,390
You can say, I'm looking for opportunities to grow and develop my skills.

1071
00:48:36,390 --> 00:48:40,590
Yes, and that sounds much more professional than just saying, I'm bored.

1072
00:48:40,590 --> 00:48:41,590
Definitely.

1073
00:48:41,590 --> 00:48:46,190
So instead of I'm bored, you can say, I'm looking for new challenges.

1074
00:48:46,190 --> 00:48:47,190
That's a great phrase.

1075
00:48:47,190 --> 00:48:49,470
It sounds positive and motivated.

1076
00:48:49,470 --> 00:48:52,550
Let's imagine someone is thinking about leaving their job.

1077
00:48:52,550 --> 00:48:54,790
What are some natural ways to express that?

1078
00:48:54,790 --> 00:48:58,470
You can say, I've been thinking about changing jobs.

1079
00:48:58,470 --> 00:49:01,070
Or I'm considering a career move.

1080
00:49:01,070 --> 00:49:02,990
That one sounds very professional.

1081
00:49:02,990 --> 00:49:05,990
You could also say, I'm exploring new opportunities.

1082
00:49:05,990 --> 00:49:07,270
I like that.

1083
00:49:07,270 --> 00:49:08,990
It doesn't sound negative at all.

1084
00:49:08,990 --> 00:49:10,950
It shows you're open to growth.

1085
00:49:10,950 --> 00:49:11,950
Exactly.

1086
00:49:11,950 --> 00:49:16,550
Now, what if someone asks, why do you want to leave your current job?

1087
00:49:16,550 --> 00:49:19,350
That's an important question, especially in interviews.

1088
00:49:19,350 --> 00:49:22,990
Yes, and your answer needs to be honest but positive.

1089
00:49:22,990 --> 00:49:26,510
For example, you can say, I'm ready for a new challenge.

1090
00:49:26,510 --> 00:49:30,830
Or I'm looking for a role that better matches my skills and goals.

1091
00:49:30,830 --> 00:49:34,670
Another good one is I'd like to take on more responsibility.

1092
00:49:34,670 --> 00:49:35,750
That's excellent.

1093
00:49:35,750 --> 00:49:37,270
It shows ambition.

1094
00:49:37,270 --> 00:49:40,910
Daniel, what about people who want better work-life balance?

1095
00:49:40,910 --> 00:49:43,230
That's a very common reason today.

1096
00:49:43,230 --> 00:49:46,630
You can say, I'm looking for better work-life balance.

1097
00:49:46,630 --> 00:49:49,150
Or I'd like a more flexible schedule.

1098
00:49:49,150 --> 00:49:51,110
Yes, especially if someone wants

1099
00:49:51,110 --> 00:49:52,870
remote or hybrid work.

1100
00:49:52,870 --> 00:49:54,670
You could also say, I'm looking

1101
00:49:54,670 --> 00:49:57,670
for a role with more flexible working arrangements.

1102
00:49:57,670 --> 00:49:59,550
That sounds very professional.

1103
00:49:59,550 --> 00:50:01,790
Now let's talk about job searching.

1104
00:50:01,790 --> 00:50:03,790
Once you decide to change your job,

1105
00:50:03,790 --> 00:50:05,270
what's the first step?

1106
00:50:05,270 --> 00:50:08,110
The first step is updating your resume.

1107
00:50:08,110 --> 00:50:11,390
Right, you can say, I need to update my resume.

1108
00:50:11,390 --> 00:50:15,910
Or I'm revising my resume to include my recent experience.

1109
00:50:15,910 --> 00:50:17,950
And don't forget the cover letter.

1110
00:50:17,950 --> 00:50:21,110
Yes, you can say, I'm writing a cover letter

1111
00:50:21,110 --> 00:50:22,270
for this position.

1112
00:50:22,270 --> 00:50:25,670
Or I customized my cover letter for each application.

1113
00:50:25,670 --> 00:50:27,470
Then comes job searching.

1114
00:50:27,470 --> 00:50:30,030
You can say, I'm currently job hunting.

1115
00:50:30,030 --> 00:50:32,950
Or, I'm applying for several positions.

1116
00:50:32,950 --> 00:50:37,110
Another useful phrase is, I found this job posting online.

1117
00:50:37,110 --> 00:50:40,390
And, I submitted my application yesterday.

1118
00:50:40,390 --> 00:50:42,550
Then comes the waiting stage.

1119
00:50:42,550 --> 00:50:46,110
Yes, and people often say, I'm waiting to hear back.

1120
00:50:46,110 --> 00:50:48,030
That's a very natural phrase.

1121
00:50:48,030 --> 00:50:50,310
Now, let's move to interviews.

1122
00:50:50,310 --> 00:50:52,070
Ah, the stressful part.

1123
00:50:52,070 --> 00:50:53,270
Very true.

1124
00:50:53,270 --> 00:50:56,030
What do people usually say before an interview?

1125
00:50:56,030 --> 00:50:57,830
I have an interview tomorrow.

1126
00:50:57,830 --> 00:51:00,310
Or I'm preparing for an interview.

1127
00:51:00,310 --> 00:51:01,550
And during the interview,

1128
00:51:01,550 --> 00:51:03,950
you need to answer questions clearly.

1129
00:51:03,950 --> 00:51:06,170
Let's practice a common question.

1130
00:51:06,170 --> 00:51:07,670
Tell me about yourself.

1131
00:51:07,670 --> 00:51:09,070
A good answer could be,

1132
00:51:09,070 --> 00:51:11,510
I have three years of experience in marketing

1133
00:51:11,510 --> 00:51:14,190
and I specialize in social media management.

1134
00:51:14,190 --> 00:51:15,910
That's clear and professional.

1135
00:51:15,910 --> 00:51:16,950
You can also add,

1136
00:51:16,950 --> 00:51:19,230
I'm currently looking for new opportunities

1137
00:51:19,230 --> 00:51:20,510
to grow my career.

1138
00:51:20,510 --> 00:51:21,950
Another question is,

1139
00:51:21,950 --> 00:51:23,870
why do you want this job?

1140
00:51:23,870 --> 00:51:28,870
You can say, I'm interested in this role because it aligns with my skills and experience.

1141
00:51:28,870 --> 00:51:34,870
Or, I'm excited about this opportunity because I want to develop my expertise in this field.

1142
00:51:34,870 --> 00:51:35,870
What about strengths?

1143
00:51:35,870 --> 00:51:38,870
You can say, I'm a strong communicator.

1144
00:51:38,870 --> 00:51:41,870
Or, I'm highly organized and detail-oriented.

1145
00:51:41,870 --> 00:51:44,870
Another good one is, I work well under pressure.

1146
00:51:44,870 --> 00:51:46,870
And weaknesses?

1147
00:51:46,870 --> 00:51:51,870
That's tricky, but you can say, I sometimes take on too much work,

1148
00:51:51,870 --> 00:51:54,190
but I'm learning to manage my time better.

1149
00:51:54,190 --> 00:51:56,430
That's honest and shows improvement.

1150
00:51:56,430 --> 00:51:59,310
After the interview, what do people usually say?

1151
00:51:59,310 --> 00:52:01,310
I think the interview went well.

1152
00:52:01,310 --> 00:52:04,990
Or I was nervous at first, but I felt more confident later.

1153
00:52:04,990 --> 00:52:07,070
And then again, waiting.

1154
00:52:07,070 --> 00:52:09,390
Yes, I'm waiting for their response.

1155
00:52:09,390 --> 00:52:12,190
Now let's imagine you receive a job offer.

1156
00:52:12,190 --> 00:52:13,230
That's exciting.

1157
00:52:13,230 --> 00:52:15,950
You can say, I received a job offer.

1158
00:52:15,950 --> 00:52:18,030
Or they offered me the position.

1159
00:52:18,030 --> 00:52:21,070
Then you respond with, thank you for the offer.

1160
00:52:21,070 --> 00:52:23,110
What if you want to discuss salary?

1161
00:52:23,110 --> 00:52:25,990
You can say, I'd like to discuss the salary.

1162
00:52:25,990 --> 00:52:28,670
Or is there any flexibility in the offer?

1163
00:52:28,670 --> 00:52:30,670
Another polite phrase is,

1164
00:52:30,670 --> 00:52:33,550
I was hoping for a slightly higher salary.

1165
00:52:33,550 --> 00:52:34,990
And if you accept?

1166
00:52:34,990 --> 00:52:37,150
I'd be happy to accept the offer.

1167
00:52:37,150 --> 00:52:39,750
Or I'm pleased to accept the position.

1168
00:52:39,750 --> 00:52:41,310
And if you decline it,

1169
00:52:41,310 --> 00:52:44,070
thank you, but I've decided to decline.

1170
00:52:44,070 --> 00:52:46,270
Very polite and professional.

1171
00:52:46,270 --> 00:52:49,430
Now comes the difficult part, resigning.

1172
00:52:49,430 --> 00:52:51,470
Yes, talking to your boss.

1173
00:52:51,470 --> 00:52:55,190
You can start with, I'd like to discuss something important.

1174
00:52:55,190 --> 00:52:57,670
Then say, I've decided to move on.

1175
00:52:57,670 --> 00:53:00,270
Or, I've accepted another position.

1176
00:53:00,270 --> 00:53:02,150
And you must give notice.

1177
00:53:02,150 --> 00:53:05,190
Yes, I'd like to give my two weeks notice.

1178
00:53:05,190 --> 00:53:07,790
Or, my last working day will be...

1179
00:53:07,790 --> 00:53:10,110
It's also important to be respectful.

1180
00:53:10,110 --> 00:53:12,670
You can say, thank you for the opportunity.

1181
00:53:12,670 --> 00:53:15,550
Or, I've learned a lot during my time here.

1182
00:53:15,550 --> 00:53:18,030
What about helping during the transition?

1183
00:53:18,030 --> 00:53:22,470
You can say, I'll do my best to complete my tasks before I leave.

1184
00:53:22,470 --> 00:53:25,110
Or I'm happy to help train my replacement.

1185
00:53:25,110 --> 00:53:26,790
That's very professional.

1186
00:53:26,790 --> 00:53:29,270
Yes, it helps you leave on good terms.

1187
00:53:29,270 --> 00:53:32,230
Now let's talk about starting a new job.

1188
00:53:32,230 --> 00:53:33,550
The exciting part.

1189
00:53:33,550 --> 00:53:36,470
On your first day, you can say, nice to meet you.

1190
00:53:36,470 --> 00:53:37,430
I'm Daniel.

1191
00:53:37,430 --> 00:53:39,350
Or I'm excited to be here.

1192
00:53:39,350 --> 00:53:42,030
You can also ask, could you show me around?

1193
00:53:42,030 --> 00:53:45,390
When learning new tasks, you can say, I'm still learning.

1194
00:53:45,390 --> 00:53:47,630
Or could you explain that again?

1195
00:53:47,630 --> 00:53:51,210
Another useful phrase is, I'm not familiar with this yet.

1196
00:53:51,210 --> 00:53:54,470
After some time, you can say, I'm getting the hang of it.

1197
00:53:54,470 --> 00:53:56,510
That's one of my favorite phrases.

1198
00:53:56,510 --> 00:53:59,750
It means you're starting to understand and feel comfortable.

1199
00:53:59,750 --> 00:54:02,390
And if everything goes well, you might say,

1200
00:54:02,390 --> 00:54:04,310
I'm glad I made this change.

1201
00:54:04,310 --> 00:54:06,870
Or, I think I made the right decision.

1202
00:54:06,870 --> 00:54:10,150
Daniel, this has been a really comprehensive discussion.

1203
00:54:10,150 --> 00:54:12,670
Yes, we covered the entire journey

1204
00:54:12,670 --> 00:54:16,190
from thinking about changing your job to starting a new one.

1205
00:54:16,190 --> 00:54:20,270
And the key message is simple. You don't need complicated English.

1206
00:54:20,270 --> 00:54:24,750
Exactly. Simple, clear, and polite phrases are enough.

1207
00:54:24,750 --> 00:54:27,830
Before we finish, let's ask our listeners a question.

1208
00:54:27,830 --> 00:54:30,350
Yes. Our question of the day is...

1209
00:54:30,350 --> 00:54:33,670
If you could change your job, what would be your main reason?

1210
00:54:33,670 --> 00:54:35,310
You can answer like this.

1211
00:54:35,310 --> 00:54:39,110
I would change my job because I want better work-life balance.

1212
00:54:39,110 --> 00:54:42,350
Or I want to learn new skills and grow my career.

1213
00:54:42,350 --> 00:54:44,870
Thank you so much for learning with us today.

1214
00:54:44,870 --> 00:54:49,670
Keep practicing, keep improving, and don't be afraid to take the next step in your career.

1215
00:54:49,670 --> 00:54:51,470
We'll see you in the next episode.

1216
00:54:51,470 --> 00:54:52,470
Goodbye, everyone!
